1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The wife of R' Joseph Teomim, was "the daughter of R. Moses Phineas Harif" who was married to "R. Joseph Teomim".  However, in "The Unbroken Chain" and in other sources, she is confused with the wife of the much yo
2 CONC unger R. Joseph Teomim, A.B.D. Bursztyn.   [He in fact was married to Sheindel, daughter of R. Zvi Hirsch Ashkenazi, A.B.D. Bursztyn.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her given name was Channa [or Anna], and she was born in Lemberg about 1692, likely the youngest child of R' Moses Phineas Harif (c1640-1702) and wife, Gela [Fegela] (Rappaport) Harif (b. c1651).  She was married to R' Joseph ["Jo
2 CONC ske"] Teomim-Frankel (b. c1695) about 1718.
