1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Here is his death record from Lemberg / Lwów: http://agadd.home.net.pl/metrykalia/300/sygn.%20671/pages/PL_1_300_671_0121.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT It gives his name as Osias Leib Horowitz. It appears that he died on 7 August 1875 and was only buried 18 days later on the 25th. Under Haus-Nro. it says "Ernsdorf bei Bielitz". Is that where he died or where he lived? I assume it
2 CONC  means he died there. Hence the long delay before his burial back home in Lemberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernsdorf is now Jaworze (Powiat Bielski), Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Bernhard Friedberg, Geschichte der Familie Horowitz. Ihr Leben und literarisches Wirken von Beginn des 16. Jahrhunderts bis auf die Gegenwart, 2nd edition, Antwerp, 1928, he was a great Torah scholar and prominent in 
2 CONC the Jewish community died on Shabbat 6th of Av 1875 in Lvov at the age of 63.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is called Schaje Leib in the marriage record of his son Samuel.
