1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The following is something strikingly astounding to know about The TaZ (Turei Zahav), which is how we generally refer to Rabbi David HaLevi, zt"l.  It is a quote from Hayom Yom compiled by the Lubavitcher Rebbe, Ra
2 CONC bbi Menachem Mendel Schneersohn, zt"l, based on talks & letters of his father-in-law, The Rebbe, Yosef Yitzchak Schneersohn. My father (The Rebbe RaShaB) wrote that he heard in the name of the Alter Rebbe that all rabbinic authors
2 CONC  until and including the Taz1 and Shach,2 composed their works with ruach hakodesh, the Divine Spirit. An individual's ruach hakodesh, as explained by Korban Ha'eida in Tractate Sh'kalim (Talmud Yerushalmi), end of ch. 3, means th
2 CONC at the mysteries of Torah are revealed to him. This comes from the aspect of chochma in its pre-revelation state.
