1 NOTE {geni:about_me} R' Herschl Zwillinger moved to Trencin megye, Hungary [now northwestern Slovakia].  He eventually settled in the community of O'Besztercze [now Stara Bystrica, Slovakia] where he was Rabbi.   His first wife was Sch
2 CONC eindl, b. c1770, d. c1803.  His second wife was Anna Frankl, b. 1775.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is seen in the following census records:
2 CONT
2 CONT Trencin megye, Hungary, 1795:  Hersch Zvillinger.
2 CONT
2 CONT O’Besztercze, Trencin megye, Hungary, 1809:  Hersll Cszvillinger -- with wife, 3 sons, 1 daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Trencin megye, Hungary, 1821:  Herschl Zvillinger -- with wife, 3 sons, 1 daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT O’Besztercze, Trencin megye, Hungary, 1828:  Herm. Czvilinger
2 CONT
2 CONT Herschl appears to have still been living in 1842, but was deceased by 1848 when his second wife, Anna (Frankl) Zwillinger, is listed in the Jewish census as a widow.
