1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abraham Teomim-Zwillinger-Pollak, b. in Lissa, 1754, d. in House No. 24, 3 Apr 1824, age 69, of pneumonia. He came with his parents to Holesov from Lissa around 1774. Hebrew writing next to his name (in old Holesov
2 CONC  records) refers to him as "Abraham, son of Meir Tzvilling" [German equivalent of the Hebrew "Teomim"]. Abraham's occupation was "kinderlehrer” — a children’s teacher.  Of note, his grandson, Leopold Tauber (1803-1887), was also a
2 CONC  Hebrew elementary school teacher.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. in Holesov, c1776, his cousin, Freydl [Rosina-Perl] [Paula] Teomim-Zwillinger, b. Lissa, 1757, d. House No. 24, 19 Dec 1835, age 78. She was the daughter of R' Isaac Teomim-Zwillinger and his wife, Chaja.
2 CONT
2 CONT List of residents with civil names – 17 Nov 1788:  “Abraham Zwilling” [translation of Hebrew writing:  “Abraham son of Meir Tzvilling”].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1819: [household #24.b] ZWILLINGER, Abraham.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1830, “wittwe Fradl” [Zwillinger] is listed as the “previous occupant” of household #24.d -- Holesov, 1830:  [household #24.d] ZWILLINGER, Markus – previous occupant:  “Fraidl, wittwe”.
