1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel Zwillinger resided first in household #14 in Holesov's Jewish quarter. Following the death of his father (Oct 1794), he and his family moved into household #8 with Samuel's mother, Barbara (c1727-1800). Samu
2 CONC el died there, 30 September 1806, age 49, of typhoid.  He is seen in Holesov records as both "Samuel Zwillinger" and "Samuel Pollak".
2 CONT
2 CONT An old Holesov document that contains his name in Hebrew-Yiddish has been translated as "Shmuel [son] Meir Zwillinger".
