1 NOTE {geni:about_me} JOSEPH ZWILLINGER, aka JOSEPH ELKAN ANTON TEOMIM, b. 1760 [fl. 1760-1765], son of Markus [Meir] Teomim-Zwillinger (1732-1794) of Holesov and his wife Barbara (c1727-1800); d. in Pest, 29 May 1836, age 76 yrs. Death
2 CONC  record: “Joseph Zwillinger, age 76 yrs., d. Pest, [household] #1278, 29 May 1836.” As a young man, he left Moravia and moved to Bosing, Pozsony, Hungary [now Pezinok, Slovakia]. He resided there for many years before moving to Aj
2 CONC karendek, Veszprem megye, about 1818. He is seen in Ajdarendek, 1821-22. Shortly following that, he moved to Pest where he is seen living in 1825.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ajkarendek, Veszprem megye, 1821: CZWILLINGER, Josefus, house dealer [“circumforaneus”], with wife, and two minor children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1825: #353 – ZWELLINGER, Josef, age 60 yrs.; wife Elisabeth, age 60 yrs.; and dau Esther, age 17 yrs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1833: #812 – ZWILLINGER, Joseph, age 72 yrs., b. Bosing; wife Elisabeth, age 70 yrs., b. Bosing, next door to BERGER, Israel, age 27 yrs., b. Atad; wife Anna, age 26 yrs., b. Bosing; son Carl, age 5 yrs., b. Pest; son Herman
2 CONC , age 3 yrs., b. Pest; and son Moritz, age 1 ½ yrs., b. Pest – two doors away from ZWILLINGER, Moritz, b. Pesth, age 14, and ZWILLINGER, Charlotte, age 15, b. Veszprem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Zwillinger was m. 1st, c1787, to Rosalia [Sara], b. c1767; d. in Bosing bef. 1818 when a granddaughter was named in her honor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Zwillinger was m. 2nd, bef. 1825, to Elisabeth, b. Bosing, c1763 [fl. 1763-1765]. She d. in Pest, c1835, age about 72.
