1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Rabbi) Salomon Teomim-Zwillinger, b. Lissa, 1767, son of R' Meir [Markus] Teomim-Zwillinger, d. in Brausberg, 16 Jun 1829, age 62.  He lived for a period of time in Sviadnov [Swadnow / Swadnof], Moravia where he m
2 CONC ay have been a rabbi or a rabbinical assessor (Dayan).  He witnessed the births of two children in Holesov, 1791 and 1793 [20 Jun 1791, the birth of his nephew, Joseph, son of Abraham Zwillinger; and 19 May 1793, the birth of his 
2 CONC wife’s nephew, Herschl, son of Salamon Pollak and Judith (Jacob) Pollak].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. Liebele Neuman, aka “Liebele Jacob”, b. Holesov, c1767, dau of Jacob Neuman.  She d. in Hotzenplotz on 1 May 1813, and is buried in Mahr. Weisskirchen [stone still standing]. They lived in both Swadnof and in House No. 11, H
2 CONC olesov, before moving to Hotzenplotz [Osoblaha] in the mid-1790s. Salomon was familianten in Hotzenplotz [now Osoblaha], but his death, which took place in Brausberg, is recorded in Mahr. Weisskirchen [Hranice] Jewish records.  
