1 NAME Rabbi Moshe Mintz - MaHaram Mintz of Altofen (Obuda - Budapest)
1 NAME //
2 GIVN
2 SURN Böhm
1 NAME משה //
2 GIVN משה
2 SURN מינץ
1 NAME הג"ר משה מינץ אב"ד אובן - ישן
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Jewish Cemetery of Óbuda
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Külso Bécsi út 369
3 ADR2 Óbuda-Békásmegyer District
3 CITY Budapest
3 CTRY Hungary
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1750
2 PLAC Minkowitz
2 ADDR
3 STAE Podolia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 AUG 1831
2 PLAC District III.
2 ADDR
3 CITY Budapest
3 CTRY Hungary
1 OCCU Óbuda chief rabbinical judge
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Moshe Mintz (1750 - 6 Elul 1831, August 15, 1831) was the Av Beit Din of Altofen (Obuda), and one of the most important Hungarian rabbis of his generation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mintz was born in Minkowitz, Podolia in 1750. He served as Rabbi in Vyshnivets and Brody, and from 1789 he became Av Beit Din and rabbi of the community of Obuda, now Budapest, the largest and most prosperous community in Hungary 
2 CONC at that time. In 1793 he became chief rabbi of the entire Pest region.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''(Óbuda, Hungary was merged with Buda and Pest on 1 January 1873; it now forms part of District III-Óbuda-Békásmegyer of Budapest. The name means Old Buda in Hungarian (in German, Alt-Ofen). The name in Croatian and Serbian for t
2 CONC his city is Stari Budim, but the local Croat minority calls it Obuda (the name "Budim" they use for the fortress in Buda). In Yiddish it is called Oben). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%93buda Wiki]''
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother-in-law was https://www.geni.com/people/R-Moses-Joshua-Heschel-Ornstein-A-B-D-Radziwillow-Rodwil-and-Tarnogrod/6000000033189917069, author of "Yam Ha-Talmud".
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1803, Mintz wrote an introduction to the book "Emek Hashave" by Rabbi Aharon Horin of Arad, one of the initiators of Reform Judaism. Mintz did not retract his support for the young man even after that and ruled that his book co
2 CONC ntained no heresy. He refrained from participating in the trial in which Horin was subsequently sentenced to destroy his work. He was one of the last Hungarian rabbis to support Horin; only in 1818 did he finally turn to him when 
2 CONC he ignored Mintz's warning not to write a responsa in support of Heichal in Hamburg, renouncing him. Later, during the quarrel of the Heichal, he forced him to retract.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a community rabbi, Mintz founded a yeshiva , a rabbinical court, and a synagogue - the most magnificent synagogue in Europe of that period, according to many. At the dedication ceremony of the synagogue, Rabbi Mintz called a se
2 CONC rmon (which was published posthumously - Dvir HaBayit), in which he compared the construction of the synagogue to the establishment of Solomon's Temple by King Solomon .
2 CONT
2 CONT His disciple and successor, Rabbi Moshe Kunitz, studied secular studies and corresponded with secular scholars, and even wrote a response in a composition identified as reform Noga Tzedek (he also wrote the book "Ben Yochai," whic
2 CONC h is sometimes mistakenly attributed to Moshe Mintz). His other disciple was Rabbi Baruch Goitein, Av Beit Din of Hedyes .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1831, following his death, the congregation of Obuda left orthodoxy to follow reformist Neolog Judaism.
2 CONT
2 CONT Münz was buried in the first Jewish cemetery of Óbuda at the northern edge of the old city. The cemetery which was opened in the 1720s was eradicated in 1950. Münz's remains were reburied in the new Óbuda Jewish cemetery in 1957. 
2 CONC His tomb has since become a place of pilgrimage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT * His son https://www.geni.com/people/Yakov-M%C3%BCnz/372249762370002953 was murdered in pogroms during the Hungarian Revolution.
2 CONT * His son https://www.geni.com/people/Josef-M%C3%BCnz-A-B-D-Tab-and-Papa-Hungary/6000000079476941142 published his writings in Shu"t MaHaram Mintz in 1827, during his father's lifetime.
2 CONT * HIs daughter Amalia married a son of https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Schlesinger/6000000002765160419, who was a brother of https://www.geni.com/people/%D7%A8-%D7%A2%D7%A7%D7%99%D7%91%D7%90-%D7%90%D7%99%D7%92%D7%A8-%D7%92%D7%9
2 CONC 9%D7%A0%D7%96/6000000000739415655.
2 CONT * A son in law https://www.geni.com/people/Shachna-B%C3%B6hm/6000000079562136079 is recorded in Dembitzer's Klilas Yoifi. Shachna's wife and children have been identified from the Krakow record indexes.
2 CONT * His daughter https://www.geni.com/people/Marie-M%C3%BCnz/372265370120013551 has been added by a descendant.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography Sources:===
2 CONT
