1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOTE:  She has been disconnected from R' Zvi Hirsch Chajes, because she could not have been married to him.  She was married to Icek Kohn in 1837, and remained married to him until her death in 1889, which was subs
2 CONC equent to the death of R' Zvi Hirsch Chajes.  Her death certificate indicates that she was a widow of Icek Kohn.  She may have been confused with a different daughter of Samuel Berenstein who was married to R' Zvi Hirsch Chajes.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT birth https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:Q2HF-7PLW
2 CONT
2 CONT census 1870 https://www.openarch.nl/ran:93CB19BF-5524-40DD-ACB1-6F01BA9F1F39
2 CONT
2 CONT Najmegen Population register 1873 : previous living place mentions Breslau (Wrocław) 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://studiezaal.nijmegen.nl/MediaViewer/Imageviewer/2279381414?HighlightQueryParams=2279381414&externalCss=%2F%2Fstudiezaal.nijmegen.nl%2Ffiles%2Fstylesheets%2Fdetail-viewer.css
2 CONT
2 CONT death https://haagsgemeentearchief.nl/archieven-mais/overzicht?mizig=210&miadt=59&miaet=1&micode=0335-01&minr=7796444&miview=inv2&mialg=9722040
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the latest edition of "The Unbroken Chain" by Neil Rosenstein, R' Zvi Hirsch Chajes, ABD Zokiew and Kalisz was married to 1) Rivka (Riva), died in Zolkiew in 1856, daughter of Solomon Przeworski and 2) Golda Cohn, dau
2 CONC ghter of R. Samuel Berenstein, ABD Amsterdam and Rebecca Reizel (daughter of R' Jacob Moses Lowenstam)
2 CONT
2 CONT There were 6 children from his first marriage: 1) Leon (Leib) Chajes, 1828-1891, 2) Haim Joachim Chajes, 1830-1886, 3) Salomon Chajes, b. 1835, 4) Wolf Chajes, 1845-1901, 5) Isaac Chajes, 1842-1901, and 6) Yita (Jitte or Jutte) Sh
2 CONC ifra, 1837-1898
2 CONT
2 CONT A footnote in Chapter 11, page 252 indicates that Zolkiew civil records for the birth of the children list their mother's name as Rivke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (3rd Edition) Volume 4, Chapter 11, pages 251-256, and Chapter 12, pages 470-471
