1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HaRav Menachem Mendl Stangen-Margolioth was the rabbi of Pińczów from about 1615 to 1635 and then became rabbi of Szydlow and afterwards became the rabbi of Przemysl.  Menachem Mendl was the son of Rabbi Yoel Feivi
2 CONC sh Stangen and Fraidchy Schmelkes.  He married Sheindel Margolioth, daughter of Moses Mordechai Margolioth, who bore him seven children, and then married the daughter of Moses Harif.
2 CONT
2 CONT Menchem Mendel was '''Av bais din Premishlan,''' Poland. (added by Margot Hilary Meyer)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His tombstone says the following:
2 CONT ''Interred the day following Passover year 412 in the small count (5412) the genius the pious the renowned MV"H (Our teacher and master the Rabbi) Menachem Mendl son of the Rabbi the pious Rabbi Yoel Feivish Stangen ZT"L and next 
2 CONC to him is buried his son the Rabbi MV"H Eliyahu Z"L. (Name and remnant Menachem Moshe Flam MV"H Menachem Mendl Margoliyos AB"D (Chief of Rabbinical Court) of Framishlan was the grandson of the Rabbi the Great Light HR"R Isaac Marg
2 CONC oliyos author of Sefer Seder Gittin AB"D (Chief of Rabbinical Court) of Framishlan And great-granson and son to... Isaac Margoliyos author of Seder Gittin AB"D Pargue Interred 23rd Nissan 412''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources for HaRav Menachem Mendl Stangen-Margolioth include:
2 CONT *[http://toladot.blogspot.com/2012/04/blog-post_14.html  '''Rabbi Menachem Mendel Rabbi Margulies Stngn Przemyshl]  תולדות ושורשים - עצי משפחה - Blog
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/10405-margolioth    '''Margolioth Family w/ Chart]  Jewish Encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=36015&st=&pgnum=602&hilite=  '''Hebrew Books]
2 CONT *[http://www.hugogold.com/Horwitz/Meg.Amuk%2047pict.pdf  '''Michael Honey Horowitz Family Chart]
2 CONT *[http://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/pinkas_poland/pol2_00424.html '''Pinkas Hakehillot Polin]: " The rabbi of Przemyśl during the 1740's [sic- should be 1640s] was Rabbi Menachem ben Rabbi Yoel Feivish Shtangin (Ashkenazi)"
2 CONT * '''The Torah Ark in Renaissance Poland: A Jewish Revival of Classical Antiquity ''' By Ilia M. Rodov page 144:
2 CONT
2 CONT “In Pińczów, the earliest evidence of a rabbi names Menachem-Mendl Stangen-Margolioth (d. 1652), who lived there from 1615 to 1635.  He was born in Germany, married a daughter of the head of the yeshiva in Kazimierz, Moses Mordech
2 CONC ai Margolioth, and after her death in 1624, married a daughter of Moses Harif, the head of the Rabbinical Court in L’viv.6”
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 On the first known rabbis of Pińczów, see Zunz, Ir ha-Zedek, 74-150ff; Friedberg, Luhot zikaron, 12 n. 10; Yoel Yakobovich-Ashkenazi, “Rabanei Pinchev le-doroteyhem” (Generations of the Pińczów rabbis) in In Pinchev togt shoyn n
2 CONC isht: Sefer zikaron le Kelihat Pinchev (Tel Aviv, 1970), 113-14 (Hebrew); Wunder Elif Margaliot, 12-16 no 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>><nowiki>----------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Menachem Mendel Margolioth was married to Schondel (aka Sheindel) Margolioth bat Harav Moshe Mordechai Halevi Margolius MiPrague (Rabbi of Krakow). Upon marrieage Menachem (born Shtengen ben Yoel feivish Stengen of PrePrzemysl and
2 CONC  Pinczow) took his wifes surname, a practice common in the revered Margolioth family.  Schondel bore Menachem seven children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He then Married bat Moses Harif and had a further seven children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==He had seven sons : 
2 CONT # Israel (married bat Abraham of Tismeritz); 
2 CONT # Samuel (Shmuel of Wilna); 
2 CONT # Mordechai Asher (married bat Kapel of Krotoshin); 
2 CONT # Nabman (Rabbi at Meseritz); 
2 CONT # Harav Eliezer of Lubmol; 
2 CONT # Harav Moshe of Tarnograd; 
2 CONT # Eliyahu Margolioth (born 1599, married Gittel); 
2 CONT # Yoel Feivish (married bat Abraham of Brest Litovak); 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==daughters 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Goldle (born circa 1593) 
2 CONT * Freudel (born circa 1596, married Juda Bruck); 
2 CONT * Edel (born circa 1610, married Isaac (Yitzchak) ben Naftali Katz; 
2 CONT * Sheindel (married menachem Madosh Auerbach (took name Margolioth).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hamaor needs to be read carefully.
2 CONT
2 CONT RMM means rabbi Moshe Mordechai, and NOT rabbi Menachem Mendel...
2 CONT
2 CONT And the tree of the mother is being followed not the father.
2 CONT
