1 NAME Leah /Gelernter/
2 GIVN Leah
2 SURN Gelernter
2 _MARNM Margolioth
2 NICK Lea Margulies
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1761
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1828
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Leah, Daughter of Abraham Gelernter, may not have been a wife of Ephraim Zalman Margolioth of Brody.   Some inconsistencies have been discovered in the latest edition of The Unbroken Chain regarding the identity of her husband(s).
2 CONT
2 CONT Chapter 7, page 182 indicates that Leah, daughter of Abraham Gelernter, was the 2nd wife of R' Efraim Zalman Margolioth of Brody, and that she was formerly the wife of R' Samuel, ABD Matzyov (Mazev) who died in 1794. However, the 
2 CONC same passage on page 182 also says to see section K of the same chapter, and in that section, on page 305, the very same Leah was indicated to be the wife of Wolf Ber Schiff, with no mention at all of either Ephraim Zalman Margoli
2 CONC oth or of R' Samuel.  Furthermore, it was also specified on page 239 that Leah was married in 1781 to R. Wolf Ber (Zeev Dov) Schiff, who had his bar mitzvah on the same day, so presumably, she was the first wife of Wolf Ber Schiff
2 CONC .  Again, on page 239 there is no indication that she was ever married to either Ephraim Zalman Margolioth or to R' Samuel.  It is possible then, that 2 different Leah's may have somehow been confused with each other. It seems lik
2 CONC ely that the Leah who married Wolf Ber Schiff in 1781 may not be the same Leah who married to R' Samuel who died in 1794, before also marrying R' Efraim Zalman Margolioth of Brody.  However, both Leah's have been identified in The
2 CONC  Unbroken Chain as being the daughter of Abraham Gelernter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (3rd Edition) Volume 3, Chapter 7, pages 182, 239, and 305
