1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Zwillinger, b. House No. 24, Holesov, 20 Jun 1791, son of Abraham and Freydl (Zwillinger) Zwillinger, died in House No. 46, 14 Jul 1830, age 39, of pneumonia. His gravestone still stands in the Holesov Jewis
2 CONC h Cemetery — “Josef ben Abraham”.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a resident of House No. 24 when he m. in Holesov, 24 Sep 1815, Hendl Hersch, b. Holesov, 1786, d. Holesov, 26 Feb 1861, age 72.  Stone still standing.  [Witness to their marriage was Michael Hersch].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Prior to his death, he had earlier lived in households #24, #22, and #44.   As his father's eldest surviving son, he was "familiant".
