1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anna [Chaja] [Tscharna] Frankl, aka “Scharloti Frankl”, b. household #32, Holesov, 20 Feb 1798, “dau of Abra: Frankl and Zartl Isack”, was named in honor of her grandmother, Anna [Chaja] Teomim-Zwillinger (1726-179
2 CONC 2).  Her birth record calls her “Sara Frankl”, erroneously switching her first name with the first name of the child entered directly above hers – Sara Wolf, b. 12 Feb 1798, listing that child as “Anna Wolf’.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She was m. 16 Aug 1814 to Selig Limon, b. household #46, 7 May 1792.  Marriage record:  “Selig Leman, age 23, household #45, and Tscharna Frankl, age 18, m. 16 Aug 1814 [witness:  Abraham Frankel].”  She was still alive when the 1
2 CONC 857 census was taken [referred to as "Anna Limon, b. 1799”], but was deceased by 1869.
