1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Rabbi) Joshua Feiwel Teomim-Fraenkel, b. Lissa, c1782; d. at Chodziesen, Kolmar, Posen [Poland], 1840.  He was a well-known Rabbi, Rabbinical Assessor, and Dayan at Chodziesen for many years.  According to the His
2 CONC tory of the Jews in Lissa, he was a close friend of the renowned Rabbi, Akiba Eger.  He is listed in a book of prominent rabbis as:  Teomim, Josua Feibel.  Known also by his civil name of Philip Frankel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. Sara Boaz, b. 1778, d. Chodziesen, 1840.  With his son Abraham, he was naturalized on 7 Jan 1835.
