1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aron Zwillinger, b. Sokal, 1810, was the son of R Salomon [Simcha] Nathan Teomim-Zwillinger, younger brother of Abraham Zwillinger (b. 1804) and younger half-brother of Benjamin Zwillinger (1787-1831).  He lived in
2 CONC  the nearby town of Cholojowa.  His wife was Mindl [Mindla].  A second wife was Hinda.  When married to her, they lived in Ickowiczow near Bobrowniki [in the Lublin region of Poland].  He was a peddler from Cholojowa but temporari
2 CONC y in Szekesfehervar, Hungary when he died in a hospital there, 22 Dec 1868, age 58, from tuberculosis.
