1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moises Zwillinger was his father's eldest son and familiant.  In 1785 and 1787, he is seen as "Moises Michl", indicating that he was the son of R' Michael Teomim-Zwillinger.  He resided in household #5, although li
2 CONC ved briefly in household #22 in 1789 and 1790.  He soon returned to household #5 where he died on 19 February 1817, "age 66".  However, he was likelier around 58 at death based on the fact that he reported his age as 25 when he wa
2 CONC s married in 1784.  His death record indicates that "withering away" was his cause of death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was familiant No. 229 in Holesov.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married in Holesov, 8 Oct 1784, to his cousin, Eva Pollak, b. Holesov, 1761, dau of R' Juda Lobl Teomim-Pollak and wife Tscharna.  Eva died in House No., 5, Holesov, on 10 July 1836, age 75.  She was a widow living in Holes
2 CONC ov in 1819 – Holesov, 1819:  [households #5.f, #22-d] ZWILLINGER, Anna.  By 1830, she is listed as the “previous occupant” of household 5.d, and was likely living with her son, Abraham, in household #22.b.
