1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was one of four daughters living in her father’s household in Vorosvar, 1821-1822, but not seen in parents’ household in 1833 [likely working/living in another family’s residence]. Pest, 1836: #702 – ZWILLINGER
2 CONC , Marc., age 60 yrs., b. Vorosvar; wife Fany, age 41 yrs., b. Brunn; dau Cathi, age 19 yrs., b. Pest; dau Anna, age 4 yrs., b. Pest; plus servant, Marie [illegible], age 13, b. Szambek. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was likely the Catharina Zwillinger working in the Heller household in 1840, but her age is erroneously given as 17 -- Pest, 1840: ZWILLINGER, Catharina, age 17 yrs. [*error for age 22 or 23], b. Vorosvar, “kochin” [cook] in h
2 CONC ousehold of Moses Heller.
