1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth record https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000141136248483
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth record calls him "Markus Pollak", b. House No. 8, Holesov, 1 Jun 1784, son of Samuel and Sara.  [Note:  Pollak was an alternate surname used by Samuel Teomim-Zwillinger.]  Markus Zwillinger had the Hebrew name of "Mordechai"
2 CONC , and was named in honor of his great-grandfather, Mordechai, father of Barbara Zwillinger.  He lived first in household #9 in Holesov's Jewish quarter.  Later, around 1818-1819, he moved to household #47.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a resident of House No. 8 when he m. 1st, in Holesov, 18 Mar 1805, Gutel Hersch, aka “Katharina Hersch”, b. Holesov, 1782.  Witnesses:  "Sam. Zwilling" and Markus Hersch.  They were the parents of eight children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  ZWILLINGER, Markus, b. 1782; wife Katharina, b. 1785; and dau Barbara, b. 1809.
2 CONT
2 CONT Markus died in Hullein on 4 May 1863, age 79, and was buried in Holesov. His stone is still standing — “Mordechaj Zwillinger, died 4 May 1863”. His wife spent her last years in the home of her son Hermann in Hullein.  Holesov, 186
2 CONC 9 — Hullein:  ZWILLINGER, Hermann, b. 1820; wife Betti, b. 1820; dau Pepi, b, 1850; son Samuel, b. 1855; son Jacob, b. 1857; and mother, ZWILLINGER, Katharina, b. 1785.
