1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob [Jakob] [Jaakov] Zwillinger, b. House No. 14, Holesov, 12 Aug 1793, youngest child of Samuel and Sara (Glata) Zwillinger, died in Holesov, after 1869. His stone is still standing in the Holesov Jewish cemeter
2 CONC y but the death date is almost indecipherable. However, a close look at the gravestone seems to indicate that he died on the 6th of July in his 80th year of age [6 July 1873].
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a resident of House No. 3, when he m. 1st, in Holesov, 31 Oct 1824, Dorothea [Dobrisch] [Deborah] [Betti] Weinberger, b. Holesov, 20 Dec 1800, d. in Holesov bet. 1857 and 1863.  Five children.  He m. 2nd, before 1869, Rache
2 CONC l / Rosa [maiden name unknown], b. Leipnik, 1823.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857: Jacob Zwillinger, born 1793, shopkeeper (retail dealer), Holesov #14; his wife, Betti, born 1799; his son, Lazar, born 1829; his son, Moses, born 13-8-1842.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869:  Jacob Zwillinger, born 1794 (error for 1793), tanner, Holesov #14; his wife, Rosi, born 1825 in Lipnik; his grandchild, Wilhelm Kapp, born Brusne, 26-2-1860, son of Moses Kapp and Salli Zwillinger.
