1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maria Zwillinger, b. Bosing, c1799 [fl. 1796-1804]; d. Pest, 4 Nov 1882, “age 86 yrs” [but, per census records, likelier, age 83 yrs. Pest death record: “Maria Grunhut geb. Zwillinger, age 86, b. Bazin [= Bosing], 
2 CONC widow of Lipot Grunhut, d. Pest, 4 Nov 1882.”  Salgotarjani, Budapest Grave:  “Grunhut Maria szul. Zwillinger, d. 1882”.   
2 CONT
2 CONT She came from Bosing to Pest prior to 1820 and is seen working that year in the Schindler household. Pest, 1820: Theresienstadt – ZVILINGER, Maria, age 20 yrs., single, b. Posing, servant/cook in household of SCHINDLER, Joseph, ag
2 CONC e 40 yrs., and wife Fetni, age 40 yrs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She m. in Pest, c1822, Leopold Grunhut, b. Pest, 1797 [fl. 1797-1799]; d. Pest, 27 Jul 1870, age 73 yrs. His death record: "Lipot Grunhut, master tailor, age 73 yrs., d. Pest, 27 Jul 1870." 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1842, Maria’s motherless niece, Regina Zwillinger (1832-1908), daughter of her brother Moises, came to live with them. She was raised by Maria and Leopold Grunhut as their own daughter. In 1857, another of Maria's orphaned niec
2 CONC es, Louise Zwillinger (b. 1837), dau of her brother Lobl, was living in her household.
