1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moises [Moritz] Zwillinger, aka “Mauritius Zwillinger”, b. Bosing, 1806, died in Buda, 1 Feb 1848, “age 38” [but actually in his 42nd year of age]. He was one of two minor children still in his father’s household [
2 CONC in Ajkarendek] in 1821-1822. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to “Who’s Who in Budapest”, Moises Zwillinger was a glazier by occupation and came to Pest from Bosing in 1826. “Moritz Zwillinger” registered as a retailer in both 1837 and 1845. In 1845, he declared that his income was
2 CONC  35 forints. He and his family resided in household #1336 in Pest’s Jewish quarter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1831/1832: ZVILLINGER, Mauritius, skilled tradesman, lives at #1036 Theresinstadt, with wife, one son, two daughters, and one servant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1833: #705 – ZWILLINGER, Moritz, age 27 yrs., b. Posing; wife, Theresia, age 26 yrs., b. Pesth; son Samuel, age 7 yrs., b. Pesth; dau Magdalena, age 5 yrs., b. Pesth; dau Rosalia, age 3 yrs., b. Pesth; and dau Regina, age ½ 
2 CONC yr., b. Pesth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1836: [pg. 151/702] ZWILLINGER, Moritz, age 30 yrs., b. Bosing; wife, Theresia, age 29 yrs., b. Pesth; son Samuel, age 10 yrs., b. Pesth; dau Magdalena, age 8 yrs., b. Pesth; dau Rosalia, age 6 yrs., b. Pesth; dau Regina, ag
2 CONC e 4 yrs., b. Pesth; plus one boarder and one servant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1838: #633 – ZWILLINGER, Moritz, with wife, three daughters, and one servant.  Also – Pest, 1839: [pg. 69/342] – ZWILLINGER, Mauritius, broker, with one son, two daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1840: ZWILLINGER, Moritz, age 34 yrs., glasaver, b. Bosing; wife, Theres, age 32, b. Pest; dau Magdalena, age 12 yrs., b. Pest; dau Rosalie, age 10 yrs., b. Pest; and dau Regina, age 8 yrs, b. Pest. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1840: [pg. 70/349] ZWILLINGER, Mauritius, broker, with one son, 2 daughters [*error for three daughters]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1842/1843: ZWILLINGER, Mauritius, merchant, with wife, one daughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 1st, c1825, Theresia [Theres], b. Pest, 1807; d. in Pest, household #269, 26 Mar 1842, age 34. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 2nd, in Pest, 9 Mar 1845, Magdalena Spitzer, b. Bosing, 1813. 
