1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moshe Babad's father,   Rabbi Yehoshua Heschel Charif (born in Vilna around 1580 and died in 5408-1648 in Krakow) was one of the students of the Maharam of Lublin and of Rabbi Yehoshua Falk.  He had many students, 
2 CONC and was known for his book '''"Meginei Shlomo"''' which included novellae on many tractates of the Talmud. Aside from this, he is known for his book of responsa '''"Pnei Yehoshua".'''
