2 CONT <p>Moshe Babad's father,   Rabbi Yehoshua Heschel Charif (born in Vilna around 1580 and died in 5408-1648 in Krakow) was one of the students of the Maharam of Lublin and of Rabbi Yehoshua Falk.  He had many students, and was known
2 CONC  for his book '''"Meginei Shlomo"''' which included novellae on many tractates of the Talmud. Aside from this, he is known for his book of responsa '''"Pnei Yehoshua".'''</p><p><p></p></p><p><p>*[http://www.geni.com/discussions/11
2 CONC 1544  '''True Story of Teivil, Moshe Babad's daughter''']</p></p><p><p>*[http://www.microtarget.com/HorowitzAssociation/Horowitz%20Rev.5.1.pdf  ''' Moshe Babad in Horowitz Family Tree''']</p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p><
