1 NAME R' Menachem Mendel Auerbach (the Younger), A.B.D. Krotoschin
1 NAME //
2 GIVN
2 SURN אוירבך
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1717
2 PLAC Krotoszyn, Greater Poland, Poland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 JAN 1760
2 ADDR
3 CITY Krotoszyn
3 STAE Greater Poland Voivodeship
3 CTRY Poland
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Menachem Mendel Auerbach succeeded his grandfather as A.B.D. Krotoschin after the death of R. Menachem Mendel Margolith in 1729.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was known as the Younger.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was leader of the Council of the Four Lands, married the daughter of R. Isaac, Parnas of Posen and Krotoschin, son of E. Samuel Katzenellenbogen, who according to family tradition, helped to finance the destitute Swedish King C
2 CONC harles X11, after his Russian defteat, so that he could reach home.
2 CONT
2 CONT He wrote approbations to Shtei HaLechem in 1733, Even HaShoham, Me'irat Einayim and Or Chachamim by R Benjamin, son of R. Saul Katzenellenbogen A.B.D. Samter and Krotoschin.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1760 and left responsa and manuscripts extant.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain, by Neil Rosenstein (1990) Volume 11, p 819, G8.2
