1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Kopelman papers:
2 CONT "At the same time that my grandmother was giving birth to my 
2 CONT mother, in another room of the house, one of her stepdaughters was also in labor, a situation 
2 CONT not lacking a certain piquancy. In this house there also lived my grandfather’s old mother, 
2 CONT Sima, after whom our Mulinka (Max’s wife, whom he called Mulinka, was also his 
2 CONT cousin) was named. This old lady, my wife’s grandmother, still saw Napoleon at the time of 
2 CONT the French invasion of Russia, on which subject there exist several anecdotes. She died when 
2 CONT my mother was already an adult and I never knew her, but Mother spoke about her often."
