1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Noakh-Dovid BLOKH's Factory
2 CONT
2 CONT The highly educated son of Sender and Malka-Reizl BLOKH – Noakh-Dovid BLOKH – founded a small spinning and fabric finishing factory in partnership with his brother Bontshe (Ben-Tzion] BLOKH on the Nowi. When the factory went bankr
2 CONC upt, Noakh-Dovid BLOKH fled to Vienna. There he became a co-worker at Vienna German newspapers and died there. His brother later again operated a small spinning factory. Here we have described the first large, but unsuccessful att
2 CONC empts by the Bialystoker Jewish aristocratic wealthy men to establish self-contained 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Page 33] 
2 CONT
2 CONT textile factories. This required a knowledge of the trade and many years of experience, such as the German manufacturers had. 
