1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This is the profile for G9.8 R' Meshullam Zalman Katzenellenpogen, ABD Kedainaia, son of G8.1 R. David Katzenellenpogen, who was born about 1690, and died about 1756.  G9.8  R' Meshullam Zalman Katzenellenpogen was
2 CONC  the father of G10.1 R. Menachem Nachum Katzenellenpogen, G10.2 R. (Moses) Mordechai Katzenellenpgogen, and G10.3 Bathsheba Rabinowitz.  He had a nephew who was also named Meshullam Zalman Katzenellenpogen (son of his brother Abra
2 CONC ham), so please don't confuse the two.
2 CONT
2 CONT G9.8 R. Meshullam Zalman Katzenellenpogen, ABD Kedainiai, succeeded his father about 1756, where he signed in the Community Records in 1758, 1760, 1762, and 1770.  He wrote approbations to Beit Yaakov Eish by R. Jacob Uri Fewer, s
2 CONC on of R. Menachem Nachum, published in Frankfurt-on-Main in 1765 and together with his brother, R. Abraham Katzenellenpogen, ABD Brest-Litovsk (while he was still in Slutsk) and his own son, R. Menachem Nachum, an approbation date
2 CONC d 27 Nisan, 1773, to Tiferet Israel by R. Israel, son of Aaron Jaffe, published in Frankfurt-on-Main, 1774.  He was a brother-in-law to R. Nachman of Keidaniai (born 1720), son of Aryey Leib, ABD Novogrudok (and his wife, Rebecca,
2 CONC  daughter of R. Simha Rappaport, ABD Dubno and Grodno).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (3rd edition) Volume 3, pages 357 and 421-429
