1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the 3rd edition of "The Unbroken Chain", by Neil Rosenstein, Volume 4 contains two references to the Wife of Shumuel Malawsky.  The first mention is in her husband's entry, in Chapter XII, page 405, and reads as
2 CONC  follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT G14.5 R. Shmuel Malawsky, ABD Ciecenow, married the daughter of R. Eleazar HaKohen (who married Breindel, sister of R. Jacob Lorbeerbaum of Lissa - see this Volume, Chapter XIII- Lorbeerbaum family).
2 CONT
2 CONT Subsequent to the above entry, their descendants are also listed on page 405.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 2nd reference to the Wife of Shmuel is in her own entry, found in Chapter XIII, page 659. In this entry, however, she is listed as the daughter of G11.2 Breindel (and her husband R. Eleazer HaKohen), '''daughter''' of G10.2 R.
2 CONC  Jacob Lorbeerbaum.  The relevant entries are as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT G10.2 R. Jacob Lorbeerbaum, known as Yaakov Lisser, born about 1760, from town of Lissa (Prussia) where he was ABD, married 1) the daughter of R. Naftali Herz of Stanislaw (see Volume Three, 694), 2) Sheindel, divorced, died in Br
2 CONC ody in 1838......
2 CONT
2 CONT G11.2 Breindel, married R. Eleazer HaKohen, born in 1796 ABD Makow Mazowiecki (north of Warsaw), Pultusk (where he wrote an approbation to Shem HaGedolim He Chadash in 1864), Plock and finally ABD Sochaczew where he died in 1883..
2 CONC ...
2 CONT
2 CONT G12.6 Wife of R. Samuel Malawsky (Mlawski), ABD Ciechanow (see Chapter XII- Landau Rabbinical family of Ciechanow).
