2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Yeshaya (Sheloh) HaLevi Horowitz grave, Tiberias. 
2 NOTE The Shla"h's tomb translation is courtesy of David Ziants ("my husband Marcel's first cousin once removed's wife's step second cousin"). 
3 CONT L0: Po nikbar 
3 CONT translation: Here is buried 
3 CONT L1: HaShla"h haKadosh 
3 CONT translation: The Holy Shla"h - (Acronym Shla"h stands for "Shnei Luchot Habrit" = "two tablets of stone" - the name of the book that he wrote.) 
3 CONT L2: Moreinu haRav, Reb Yeshayahu ben haRav Avraham haLevi Horowitz tzatz"al 
3 CONT translation: Our teacher the Rav, Reb Yeshayahu son of the Rav Avraham the levi Horowitz, may the righteous one be remembered for a blessing 
3 CONT L3: Shimesh av-bet-hadin b'kehillot gedolot b'eiropa 
3 CONT translation: He served as the Head of the Bet Din in (various) large communities in Europe 
3 CONT L4: Alah miPraag l'Eretz Yisrael b'shnat hay-shin-pay-aleph 
3 CONT translation: He made aliya from Prague to the Land of Israel in the year 5371 (=1620/1621) 
3 CONT L5: Kihain k'rav shel kehillot Yerushalayim, Tzefat v'Tiveria 
3 CONT translation: He held the positions as rav of the communities of Yerushalayim, Tzefat and Tiveria 
3 CONT L6: Chibair sepharim "Shnei Luchot Habrit" v'achairim 
3 CONT translation: He wrote the books "Shnei Luchot Habrit" and others 
3 CONT L7: Niphtar b'Tiveria b'yud-aleph Nissan b'shnat hay-shin-tzadi 
3 CONT translation: He passed away in Tiberias on the 11th of Nissan in the year of 5390 
3 CONT L8: Tihiyeh nishmato tzror b'tzror hachaim 
3 CONT translation: May his soul be bound in the bond of life.
2 NOTE Can anyone please photograph well the top of tomb in close-up, and translate into English to accompany this page?
