1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *[http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=36015&st=&pgnum=602&hilite=  '''Hebrew Books]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Yoel Feivish Stangen was the son Itzchak Stangen.  Several sources indicate that he was born in Germany likely around 1520-1540.  [http://www.hugogold.com/Horwitz/Meg.Amuk%2047pict.pdf One researcher] indicates specifically 
2 CONC that he was born in the town of Jűlich near Koln (Cologne).  Yoel  married Fraidchy Schmelkes, the daughter Yehoshua Schmelkes and is the father of HaRav Menachem Mendl Stangen-Margolioth rabbi of Pińczów and later of Prezmysl.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Unbroken Chain", by Dr. Neil Rosenstein, page 451
2 CONT >''G6.6 R' Isaac Katz, Darshan of Prague and Lublin, ABD of Stepan married Edel, daughter of R. Menachem Mendel, son of Joel Margolis-Schotengen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Yoel Feivish is also referenced on the tombstone of his son Menechem Mendel which states:
2 CONT
2 CONT Although generally spelled as שטנגן in Hebrew, several variants in Roman characters exist depending on the source, including Stangen, Schtengen and Schotengen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Yoel Feivish Stangen is mentioned in the following sources (primary and secondary):
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain, by Dr. Neil Rosenstein: Page 451 Chapter V - Katz, Amsel, Parnas:
2 CONT “G6.6 R' Isaac Katz, Darshan of Prague and later A.B.D of Stepan in Volhynia. He also was elected Darshan of Lublin and married Edel, daughter of R' Menachem Mendel, son of Joel Margolis-Schotengen.”
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/pinkas_poland/pol2_00424.html Pinkas Hakehillot Polin] " The rabbi of Przemyśl during the 1740's [sic- should be 1640s] was Rabbi Menachem ben Rabbi Yoel Feivish Shtangin (Ashkenazi)"
2 CONT
2 CONT The Torah Ark in Renaissance Poland: A Jewish Revival of Classical Antiquity  By Ilia M. Rodov page 144.
2 CONT
2 CONT “In Pińczów, the earliest evidence of a rabbi names Menachem-Mendl Stangen-Margolioth (d. 1652), who lived there from 1615 to 1635.  He was born in German, married a daughter of the head of the yeshiva in Kazimierz, Moses Mordecha
2 CONC i Margolioth, and after her death in 1624, married a daughter of Moses Harif, the head of the Rabbinical Court in L’viv.6”
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 On the first known rabbis of Pińczów, see Zunz, Ir ha-Zedek, 74-150ff; Friedberg, Luhot zikaron, 12 n. 10; Yoel Yakobovich-Ashkenazi, “Rabanei Pinchev le-doroteyhem” (Generations of the Pińczów rabbis) in In Pinchev togt shoyn n
2 CONC isht: Sefer zikaron le Kelihat Pinchev (Tel Aviv, 1970), 113-14 (Hebrew); Wunder Elif Margaliot, 12-16 no 16.
