1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Paternity conflicts with: https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Moses-Katz-ABD-Lutsk/6000000081359208122
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the year 5363 (1603), served as the Rabbi of Lutsk one of the greatest rabbis of his generation, HaGaon R' Moshe son of R' Yehudah HaCohen Shapira, grandson of the well known Gaon, R' Yitzchak Shapira, president of the court o
2 CONC f the holy community of Krakow. HaGaon R' Moshe, the Rabbi of Lutsk, was the son-in-law of R' Shaul Wahl, the Polish "King," who carried the crown of Poland on his head for one night. There are many legends about this matter in th
2 CONC e history of the Jews of Poland, and R' Shaul was undoubtedly the leader, and the "lobbyist," of the Jews of Poland and Lita in that generation. From Lutsk, HaGaon R' Moshe moved to serve as the Rabbi of the Krakow region. He wrot
2 CONC e the book, Questions and Answers Maharam[3], which remained in a manuscript and was not printed. There is consent from him on the book, Mekor Chachimim [The Source of Sages], which was printed together with the consents of famous
2 CONC  Geonim, the Shelah and Ba'al Halevushim[4]. He passed away in the year 5377 (1617)." https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/lutsk1/lut295.html
