1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Shlomo Englard, "Shibushim nefotzim be-megilot yuchsin III" [Common distortions in genealogy], Tzfunot 19 (1992), 86-87 demonstrates that there is no evidence that the father-in-law of Meir Rappaport was Nachman Sc
2 CONC htrenzl. See the attached.
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT From Dubno Yizkor Book: "For eleven years (1663-1674), the Rabbinical seat in Dubno was held by the great, renowned Gaon of his generation, Our Rabbi Naḥman Hacohen Liptzis, who was the Rabbi of Lwów (Lemberg, Lviv, Lvov, et. al.)
2 CONC , Kremenets, (Kremenitz), Chelm, and Belz. He was the grandchild of the Gaon Our Teacher and Rabbi Gershon Ha-Cohen Rapa of Porto, a scion of the family of Rabbi Moshe of Speyer, known as Liptzis after his mother the wealthy Mrs. 
2 CONC Liptzis, the grand-daughter of the Gaon Rabbi Yitzḥak Shrentzel...” https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/dubno/dub061.html  This quote asserts that Nachman Lifshitz is the grandson of Yitzach, meaning his mother has to be the daughter
2 CONC  of one of the two sons of Yitzach Shrentzel, Nachman or Mordechai, or the daughter of Yitzach Shrentzel's only known daughter, (name unknown). Elsewhere, Jacobi in his Rapaport Family draft (Char M, # 13.1) asserts that Nakhman b
2 CONC  Yitzach Shrentzel's daughter Lifshe is the mother of Nakhman Lifshits. So there is some evidence supporting the proposition.
