1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "The new president [of Council of Four Lands], Abraham, son of Hayim, was the second member of the
2 CONT Halperin family to hold the office [my note: the first was https://www.geni.com/people/Moshe-Heilperin-of-Poznan/383933584620011556]. He was well connected to the Jewish political elite through his family ties: his father, Hayim, 
2 CONC was a stepson of Abraham Isserles; and his son, Jacob Hayim, married Hayah, daughter of Abraham Isaac Fortis. Abraham himself had represented Lublin in the council since 1724." https://muse.jhu.edu/article/846614 (p. 132). The log
2 CONC ic implemented on GENI is that Hayim was step-son of Abraham Isserles because his biological father, also Hayim, died prior to his son's birth (his son was named in honor of the deceased father). His biological mother re-married t
2 CONC o Abraham b. Ysroel Isser. This coincides with the assertion made by Jacobi in the Heilprin Farmily draft that Chaim's widow married his nephew (Heilprin Family draft, Chart (S2), 12.1m; see also Jacobi Papers, Volume 1, p. 135, 1
2 CONC 1.2, 11.4m, 12.1 and 12.1m. Chaim's nephew, Avraham Abli (https://www.geni.com/people/Avraham-%D7%91%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%9E%D7%A1-%D7%9E%D7%99%D7%99%D7%96%D7%9C%D7%99%D7%A1-Parnas/6000000217343052846), is the son of Chaim's sister (nam
2 CONC e not yet known): https://www.geni.com/people/NN-Heilprin-Meisels/6000000217354513826, Further confirmation of this sequence of events is being sought. (03 APR 2025) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
