1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -------------------- http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ephraim_Zalman_Margolioth
2 CONT
2 CONT Ephraim Zalman Margolis (December 19, 1762–August 24, 1828) (Hebrew: אפרים זלמן בן מנחם מרגליות‎) was a Galician rabbi born in Brody.
2 CONT
2 CONT He received his Talmudic education at different yeshivas, in which he distinguished himself for the acuteness of his intellect and for his astonishing memory. His correspondence with Ezekiel Landau and other leading Talmudists soo
2 CONC n gained for him a high reputation. He established a banking-house which proved so successful that within a short time he became quite wealthy. In 1785 he published his responsa entitled Bet Hadash ha-Hadashot, and in the followin
2 CONC g year the rabbis of Brody elected him one of their number. Being of independent means, he opened in his house a yeshivah of which he was the head; several of his pupils became eminent rabbis.
2 CONT
2 CONT He published the following works:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bet Efrayim (2 vols., Lemberg, 1809-10), commentary on parts of the Shulchan Aruk, Yoreh De'ah:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=8310&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=19314&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Bet Efrayim (4 parts, ib. 1818), responsa on the four parts of the Shulchan 'Aruk:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=19558&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=642&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=631&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=641&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=61&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=1348&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Oration at the funeral of Rabbi Meir Kristianopoler (ib. 1815)
2 CONT
2 CONT Yad Efrayim (Dubno, 1820), commentaries on Shulchan Aruk, Orach Chayim
2 CONT
2 CONT Sha'are Efrayim (ib. 1820), on the rules pertaining to the reading of the Law
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=24998&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=34320&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Yad Efrayim (Zolkiev, 1823), extensive commentaries on the names of men and of women to be employed in letters of divorce:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=24607&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Shem Efrayim (Berdychev, 1826), commentary on the Torah
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=35241&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Matteh Efrayim (Zolkiev, 1834), on the ritual laws to be observed from the beginning of the month of Elul until after the Feast of Tabernacles, as well as on the regulations regarding the Kaddish of orphans
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=14072&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=9158&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=33305&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=33306&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=33307&pgnum=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Zera' Efrayim (Lemberg, 1853), commentary on the Pesikta Rabbati
2 CONT
2 CONT Many other works by him are still in manuscript (as of 1906).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogyindexer.org/view/Nachtraege/Nachtraege%20-%200337.pdf and http://genealogyindexer.org/view/Nachtraege/Nachtraege%20-%200338.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT 94. Margulies Salomon   Merc. Prot. IV, Lit. M, Tern. 3, fol. 30; V, Lit. M, Tern. 2, fol. 15 received on 22nd April 1817 the wholesale permit. On 18th September 1817 was protocoled the W. W.  contract signed between the owner and
2 CONC  Jakob P. Margulies, Simon Dische and Ascher Barbasch for the period of six years of equal profit and loss after measure of the total amount introduced of 360,000 Fl. against liability in solidum as well as the business directorsh
2 CONC ip of Salomon Margulies, Jakob P. Margulies, Simon Dische and Ascher Barbasch.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13th June 1818 Salomon Margulies & Comp. applied for protocoling of the procura granted to Markus M. Byk. On 14th November 1821, Salomon Margulies & Comp. recorded the dissolution contract with Simon Dische and Ascher Barbasch.
2 CONC  On 17th March 1822 an application was made for protocoling of the procura extended to Hirsch Beer, which was granted for six months. On 22nd December 1823 the business requested protocoling of the same procura again, which was ag
2 CONC ain approved with the date to 29th August 1824.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 5th January 1828, Salomon Margulies applied for protocolling of the dissolution contract with Jakob Perlmann Margulies, who had in the meantime died, mentioned were: a declaration of abeyance of the inheritance in favour of the
2 CONC  widow from the side of the daughter of the late Civie Derblich and the son Moses Perlmann Margulies; declaration of the widow, that she would accept liability for the trade creditors. On the declaration of S. Margulies and proof 
2 CONC of the balance sheet, on 20th May 1828 the continued running of the old firm Salomon Margulies & Comp. was approved.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 3rd August 1828 Salomon Margulies died in his home community of Brody.''' On 22nd September 1828 the widow Lea Margulies declared, that she desired the wholesale business of her spouse to be carried on by the procura manager
2 CONC  Markus M. Byk, for which she was ordered to prove within three months the acquisition and ownership of a wholesale licence. According to the magistrate of Brody, two thirds of the inheritance went to the son Chaim Leib Margulies,
2 CONC  one third to the daughter Sima Horowitz. The widow was assured of the use. After the ending of the liquidation, on 10th May 1830 the deletion of the wholesale licence as well as the company and procura were effected.
2 CONT
2 CONT Efraim Salman Margulies, the acquirer of the wholesaling, was an exceptional learned man and author of many rabbinical scriptures. He did not strive to be a rabbi and managed his wholesale business in Brody and from 1817 a similar
2 CONC  one in Vienna. Regarding the aquired Tolerance in Vienna see completely the extract of the files in Pribram II, page 613 f.f..... (the request of a certain Sal. Margulies from Brody..."). Margulies lived in Brody and let his firm
2 CONC  be run by Brody persons, who lived under the Tolerance in Vienna. The shareholders were all from Brody. Regarding his personality and the Viennese business, compare Saul Chajes, Rabbi Efraim Margulies, a tolerated wholesaler in V
2 CONC ienna, in "The Jewish World" of 31st May 1929. Regarding his son Chaim Löb Margulies, who acquired a wholesaling privilege in 1830, see further under number 133. 
