1 NOTE {geni:about_me} הרב הגאון המפורסם מו"ה אריה ליבוש הכהן ז"ל, אשר היה אב"ד דק"ק עיר חדש סמוך לוורשא ולסוף ימיו נתקבל לאב"ד בק"ק שדה חדש. הובא שו"ת ברית אברהם חלק או"ח סימן י"ח סכ"ד.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the Neustadt aka Novy Miasto, (which was once adjacent to Warsaw and is now part of Warsaw)
2 CONT
2 CONT This part of the tree is from the book TIferet Shlomo of 1866 written by Shlomo haCohen Rabinovich d1866, (https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Shlomo-Rabinowicz-of-Radomsk-Tife...). He was the grandson of Aryeh Leyb HaCohen Rabinovi
2 CONC ch and the the grandson of Eleazar HaKohen Rabinowitz. The book was published three years later in 1869. So it would seem this is well within the personal knowledge of the author of Tiferet Shlomo. This part of the tree is based o
2 CONC n the following description at the beginning of Tiferet Shlomo.
2 CONT
2 CONT "rabbi solomon the son of the renowned hasid dov tzvi hakohen from wloszczowa the son of the renowned gaon
2 CONT
2 CONT arye leibus the kohen . Who was a.b.d in the holy community New Town near to warsaw and near end of his days accepted abd of holy community new field [ quoted in the book brit abraham ] son of renowned great rabbi Eleazar abd of "
2 CONC Vaydislov"
2 CONT
2 CONT [quoted in the book shemen rokeach] son in law of Arye Leib abd of Zamoshtsh
2 CONT
2 CONT And this rav the gaon Arye Leib of New Field mentioned above was the son in law of the great rav renowned in his generation solomon
2 CONT
2 CONT abd Pintshov [ and in book shem hagdolim solomon renowned in his generation son of benjamin zev wolf abd tshikatchin son
2 CONT
2 CONT of tzvi tzazmir son in law of the ReMa son of benjamin of pozna son in law of Natan Spira author of Megale Amukot"
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT הרב הגאן המפורסם מו"ה אריה ליב אב"ד דק"ק זאמוטש
