1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Babeth [Brauna] [Betti] Zwillinger, b. household #46, 12 Nov 1818, “dau of Joseph Zwillinger and Hendl Hersch” ; d. in Holesov, 17 Apr 1880, age 62 – d. in Holesov, 17 Apr 1880, age 62 – gravestone still standing: 
2 CONC “Betti Ochs – in Hebrew, Mrs. Brauna Ochs, died 6 Ijar 5640 [17 April 1880].” 
2 CONT
2 CONT She m. in Holesov, Moravia, 27 Sep 1841, widower Manassas Ochs, b. “Martinitz” [Holesov], 1781 but possibly 1771; d. in Holesov, bet. 1852-1857. He was at least 37 years older than her. Marriage record:  “Manasses Ochs, age 60, fa
2 CONC miliant No. 66, widower, and Betti Zwillinger, age 22, dau of familianten Joseph Zwillinger, m. in Martinitz, 27 Sep 1841 [witnesses:  Markus Zwillinger and Joseph Low, familiant].”  
2 CONT
2 CONT [His previous marriage was in Holesov, 16 Dec 1818, to Judith Lowy, b. Holesov, 1788, d. Holesov, 28 Dec 1840.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  [household #83c.] ZWILLINGER, Hendl, b. 1786, widow; her daughter, OCHS, Betti, b. 1818, widow; grandson, OCHS, Josef Moses, b. 1852; granddaughters, OCHS, Hanni, b. 1843, and OCHS, Katti, b. 1844.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869: [Stadtgemeinde – pg. 705] OCHS, Betti, b. 1818, widow; dau Katti, b. 1846, ledig; son Josef, b. 1852; granddaughter, OCHS, Lotti, b. 1869.  
