1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ignatz Herschel [Isack Herschl] [Jicchak Cvi] [Ajcik Hers] Zwillinger, b. House No. 46, Holesov, 22 Dec 1822, son of Joseph and Hendl (Hirsch) Zwillinger, died in Holesov, 25 Mar 1894, in his 72nd year of age. Grav
2 CONC estone still standing – “Here lies Herr Ignatz Zwillinger, died 25 March 5654 [1894], age 72”. [He is buried next to his sons Joseph and Markus].
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. c1852, Josefa [Jocheved] [Pepi] Beer, b. Holesov, 28 Oct 1826, dau of Lion [Lobl] and Gutrid (Wolf) Beer.  She d. in Holesov, 22 Dec 1889, age 63.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth record lists him as “Herschl”:  https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000141947892966
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  ZWILLINGER, Ignac, b. 1826, of Holesov #34; his wife Pepi, b. 1829; son Josef, b. 1853; daughters Zili, b. 1855, and Netti, b. 1857.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869:  ZWILLINGER, Ignac, b. 1822, merchant, of Holesov #34; his wife Peppi, b. 1826; sons, Josef Bernard, b. 1853, Leopold, b. 1865, and Markus, b. 1869; daughters, Zilli, b. 1855, Netti, b. 1857, Rosa, b. 1859, Johanna,
2 CONC  b. 1863, and Sali, b. 1867.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1880:  [pg. 111] ZWILLINGER, Ignatz, b. Holleschau, 1823; wife Pepi, b. Holleschau, 1825; son Josef, b. Holleschau, 1853, ledig; dau Rosi, b. Holleschau, 1859, ledig; dau Hani, b. Holleschau, 1863; son Leopold, b. Hollesc
2 CONC hau, 1865; son Max, b. Holleschau, 14 Jul 1869; and dau Ernestine, b. 1872.  [Inserts:  “Max Zwillinger, b. Holleschau, 14 Jul 1869, son of Isak Herschl Zwillinger and Pepi geb. Beer”; “Leopold Zwillinger, b. Holleschau, 16 Nov 18
2 CONC 65, son of Isak Herschl Zwillinger and Pepi geb. Beer”.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1890:  [pg. 78] ZWILLINGER, I. H., b. Holesov, 22 Dec 1822, widower; son Leopold, b. 16 Apr 1865; dau Ernestine, b. 27 May 1872; son-in-law, HAAS, Josef, b. 18 Oct 1853; his wife Hani, b. 7 Nov 1863; and their dau Clara, 
2 CONC b. 16 Jul 1887.  
2 CONT
2 CONT His obituary was published in the Neue Frei Presse, Vienna, 27 Mar 1894:  “Ignatz Zwillinger … died Holesov, 25 Mar 1894, survived by children Cacilie Beer, Netti Fried, Johanna Haas, Leopold Zwillinger, and Ernestine Zwillinger; 
2 CONC by sons-in-law, Carl Beer, Eduard Fried, Josef Haas, and David Beer (fiancé of Ernestine); and by grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hebrew writing on his gravestone:
2 CONT
2 CONT ... בשט* חי אדר שני צל עובר חיי האדם עלי זו האדמה לפק י*צחק יצאת לשוח תוך עצי חגן צ*חק לפניך יהלך שמל אורך יופיע ח*וג שמים עלית רוחך עוף הגביה ק*רנך תרום בכבוד כאשר לישרים יתן צ*אציך אם מר יבכיון כי יפקדון מושבין ב*נועם מוסרך משם 
2 CONC הלא כה דבריך י*קירי צ*דיק ב*אמונתו י*חיה תמים פעלו ז*את המנוחה לעובד שדמת חסד אדמתו צ*וה ו*י*הי שרפים עומדים ממעל ל*ו ל*עת י*קיצו נ*רדמים ג*אולת ע*ולם ר*אשיתו*
