1 NOTE {geni:about_me} PLEASE NOTE:  Hersch Wolf Zwillinger did not die in 1897 -- it was his cousin, https://www.geni.com/people/Wolf-Zwillinger/6000000109432985827 (1836-1897) of Sokal, who died that year. The two men have often been c
2 CONC onfused with each other. Hersch Wolf Zwillinger was still alive in 1900, but deceased by 1910.  Unfortunately, while Tartakow Jewish birth and marriage records are available for online research, Tartakow Jewish death records are n
2 CONC ot. Hersch Wolf Zwillinger resided in Tartakow [Tartakiv] for his entire life, and is seen consistently in Jewish records as "Hersch Wolf Zwillinger" or "Hersz Wolf Zwillinger".  He is never referred to in any of those entries as 
2 CONC "Harry Swillinger".
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Hersch Wolf Zwillinger, b. Sokal, 1836, son of Abraham Leib Zwillinger and his 2nd wife, Henie Gitel Zwillinger, lived in Tartakow and died there between 1900 and 1910.  He m. in Tartakow, 10 Jun 1864, Rachel Furman, b. Tartakow, 
2 CONC 1839, dau of Juda and Leie Furman.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Tartakow Jewish marriage records:  “Hersch Wolf Zwillinger, age 28, and Rachel Furman, age 25, m. Tartakow, 10 Jun 1864 [witnesses:  Abraham Leib Zwillinger and Lissa Kram].”
