1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wolf Lippe, aka Wilhelm Lippe, Volf Lippe, Farkas Lippe, was born in Pucho, Trencin megye, Hungary [now Puchov, Slovakia] on 20 Jun 1792.  He became a rabbi in Pucho and lived there until around 1840.  He and his f
2 CONC amily then moved to Gynogyos, Heves megye, Hungary where he was appointed Chief Rabbi.  He died in Gyongyos on 9 Jan 1851, age 68 years.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Death record:  https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CS87-M9N2-L?i=574&cat=260882
2 CONT
2 CONT R' Wolf Lippe was married to Amalie Zwillinger (1798-1870), a member of the well-known Rabbinical TEOMIM family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gyöngyös, Heves megye, Hungary, 1848: LIPPE, Farkas, age 55, b. Puka [Pucho]; son, Moricz, age 26, b. Puka; son, David, age 24, b. Puka; son, Simon, age 22, b. Puka; son, Edvard, age 19, b. Puka; son, Markus, age 13, Puka
2 CONT
2 CONT [Please note:  Rabbi Wolf Lippe’s wife and daughters were not included by the census taker.]
