1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He went from Lissa to Moravia where he was a rabbi, then from there to Bohemia.  On 8 Oct 1784, he witnessed the marriage of his son, Moises, to Ewa Teomim-Pollak (in Holesov).  Hebrew writing next to his name has 
2 CONC been translated as "Jechiel b. M' Hillel".  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was still alive in July 1785 when he witnessed the birth of his grandson, Wolf, in Holesov.  Handwriting after his name (largely illegible) seems to suggest he was in "Bohmen" [Bohemia] at the time.  He was deceased by Dec 1789
2 CONC  when another grandson was named in his honor.
