1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Named in honor of his great-grandfather, R' Malkiel [Michael] Hillel Teomim-Zwillinger. He was familiant #71 in the Jewish community.
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. in Holesov, 27 Feb 1881 [stone still standing].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  [household #6] WEINREB, Michael, b. 1819; wife Netti, b. 1820; son Heinrich, b. 1850; and son Bernard, b. 1856.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869:  [ppg. 21-24] WEINREB, Michael, b. 1823; wife Netti, b. Tobitschau, 1826; son Joachim, b. 1850 [“in Pest”]; son Isak Bernard, b. 1856; son Julius, b. 1858; plus others including ROSENFELD, Aron, b. 1845; GROSS, Bern
2 CONC ard, b. 1851; and ADLER, Wilhelm, b. 1853.  [Inserts:  “Joachim Weinreb, b. 22 Nov 1850, son of Michael Weinreb and Netti geb. Deutsch”; “Isak Bernard Weinreb, b. 16 Nov 1856, son of Michael Weinreb and Netty geb. Deutsch”; “Juliu
2 CONC s Weinreb, b. 17 Sep 1858, son of Michael Weinreb and Netty geb. Deutsch”.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 1st, in Holesov, 4 Nov 1844, Sara Ehrlich, b. Holesov, 20 Jun 1819, dau of Abraham Ehrlich.  Marriage record:  “Michael Weinreb, age 25, familiant No. 71, son of familianten No. 190 Isack Weinreb and wife Rosi geb. Zwillinge
2 CONC r, and Sara Ehrlich, age 23, dau of familiant No. 187 Abraham Ehrlich and Bertha geb. Adler, m. 14 Nov 1844 [witnesses:  Isack Weinreb and Abraham Ehrlich].”  This marriage ended in divorce.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 2nd, in Holesov, 23 Feb 1849, Nany [Netti] Deutsch, b. Tobitschau, 1820-1826.  Marriage record:  “Michael Weinreb, age 29, familiant No. 71, son of familiant No. 190 Isak Weinreb and Rosl geb. Zwillinger, and Nany Deutsch, a
2 CONC ge 27, dau of Regina Deutsch ‘aus Tobitschau”, m. 22 Feb 1849.”  She may have been the “Channa Weinreb” who died in Holesov in 1891, and whose stone is still standing.
