1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She lived with Gabriel Lachs of Holesov, b. household #29, 13 May 1812, son of Juda and Judith (Klein) Lachs – probably had a religious wedding about 1841, but – because Gabriel was a younger son – had no ability t
2 CONC o have a civil marriage.  Their children were legitimatized on 16 Apr 1866 shortly after Gabriel and Julie were legally married [following the relaxation of the Familiant Laws].  In 1869, they were listed in census records as husb
2 CONC and and wife.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabriel Lachs d. in Holesov on 26 Apr 1888, age 75. Julie (Zwillinger) Lachs d. there on 26 Apr 1889, age 72. Their gravestones are still standing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857: [household #93b.] LAX, Gabriel, b. 1812, living with ZWILLINGER, Juli, b. 1818, and their illegitimate children, Juda, b. 31 Jul 1842; Moritz, b. 1844; Ascher, b. 1847; Isak, b. 1853; Leopold, b. 1857; and Judit, b.
2 CONC  1852.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869: [ppg. 250-252] LACHS, Gabriel, b. 1812; wife Juli, b. 1817; son Abraham, b. 1848; dau Judith, b. 1851 [in Wsetin]; son Isak, b. 1853 [in Plchstand (?), Mahren]; son Leopold, b. 1857, plus EHRLICH, Rosi, b. 1793, led
2 CONC ig; and STEINHART, Sara, b. 1814, widow.   [Inserts:  Isak Lachs, b. 13 Oct 1853, son of Gabriel Lachs and Julie geb. Zwillinger; Leopold Lachs, b. 21 Oct 1857, son of Gabriel Lachs and Julie geb. Zwillinger].
