1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moses Joachim [Mose Chajim] [Moritz] Klopper was b. in Holesov, 1834, the son of Hindl Klopper and Abraham Zwillinger.  Even though his parents had wed in a Jewish ceremony, their marriage was not legally recognize
2 CONC d due to the Familiant Law restrictions.  [Abraham Zwillinger was a younger son, and was not eligible to marry.]  Thus, Moses Joachim Klopper and all of his siblings were officially illegitimate.  After the Familiant Laws were rel
2 CONC axed (c1850), many couples in this same predicament were legally married and then had their children legitimatized.  But, unfortunately for Moses Joachim Klopper and his only surviving sister Eva, both of their parents were deceas
2 CONC ed by then -- Hindl Klopper in 1844, Abraham Zwillinger in 1849.  They therefore remained legally illegitimate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Joachim Klopper (alias Zwillinger) d. in Holesov, 18 Mar 1918, age 84.  Gravestone still standing.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. Sara [Serl] [Sali] Limon, b. Holesov, 14 Nov 1829, dau of Selig and Anna [Tscharna] (Frankl) Limon.  She d. in Holesov, 6 Dec 1908:  “Sali / Sara Klopper, age 79 yrs., 2 mos., wife of Moses Joachim Klopper, d. Holesov, 6 Dec
2 CONC  1908.”    
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov 1857: [household #33a] KLOPPER, Moses, b. 1825 [*error for 1834], ledig; and KLOPPER, Eva, b. 1839, ledig.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869: [Stadtgemeinde – pg. 709] KLOPPER, M. Joachim, b. 1832; wife Sali, b. 1830; son Leopold, b. 1866; and dau Hani, b. 1868.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1880:  [ppg. 229-231] KLOPPER, Moses J., b. Holleschau, 1834; wife Sali, b. Holleschau, 1832; dau Hani, b. Holleschau, 1868; son Adolf, b. Holleschau, 1871; son Sigmund, b. Holleschau, 1873; son Nathan, b. Holleschau, 186
2 CONC 6; + OCHS, Czarnna, b. Holleschau, 1820, widow; + MORGENSTERN, Max, b. Strassnitz, 1870.   [Inserts:  Adolf Klopper, b. Holleschau, 1 Mar 1871, “son of Moritz Klopper and Saly geb. Limon”; Nathan Klopper, b. Holleschau, 30 Apr 186
2 CONC 6, “son of Moses Joachim Klopper and Sara geb. Limon”].
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1900:  KLOPPER, Moses Joachim, b. Holesov, 4 Jul 1835; wife Rosalia, b. Holesov, 7 Oct 1832; dau Johanna, b. Holesov, 9 Mar 1868; and son Sigmund, b. Holesov, 12 Feb 1873.  
