1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob Zwillinger lived in Budapest until 1886 when he moved to Vienna.  He resided in Vienna for the remainder of his life and died there on 29 December 1910, age 58.  He was buried in Vienna's central cemetery on 
2 CONC 1 January 1911.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vienna Jewish Marriage Record: “Jacob Zwillinger, b. Budapest, 11 Nov 1852, son of Herman and Fanni (Strasser) Zwillinger, and Adelheid Bensinger, b. Mannheim, 5 Jan 1854, dau of Moriz and Maria Anna (Bodenheimer) Bensinger, m. in
2 CONC  Vienna, 16 Dec 1884 [Leopold Zwilling, H. Zwillinger]"   
2 CONT
2 CONT Neue Freie Presse -- 31 December 1910 (death notice)  JAKOB ZWILLINGER died Wien, 30 December 1910... survived by wife Adele Zwillinger geb. Bensinger; by children Carl, Irene, Edith, Paul, and Oskar; and by two sisters Rosa Fried
2 CONC mann and Bertha Bohm.
