1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Holesov death record:  “Israel Deutsch, age 93 yrs., 6 months, d. Holesov, household #3, 4 Jun 1901.”  He was familiant.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He acquired House No. 3 in the 1830s from Elisabeth Skrainka.  Holesov, 1830:  [household #3b] – 2. – SKRAINKA, Elisabeth.  Subsequent head-of-household:  DEUTSCH, Israel.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  [household #3] DEUTSCH, Israel, b. 1806, wife Eva, b. 1808, son Moritz, b. 18 Sep 1840, dau Julia, b. 1839, and dau Karolina, b. 1843.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869:  [pg. 11] DEUTSCH, Israel, b. 1809, widower; son Moses, b. 1841; and dau Lotti, b. 1844.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1880:  [pg. 22] House #3 -- DEUTSCH, Asriel, b. Holleschau, 1808; son-in-law, STRAUSS, David, b. Ung Ostrau, 1846; his wife, STRAUSS, Lotti, b. Holleschau, 1843; their son, Moses Samuel, b. Holleschau, 1876; and their dau
2 CONC , Eva, b. Holleschau, 1880.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1890:  STRAUSS, David, b. Ung Ostra, 1846; wife Lotti, b. Holleschau, 1843; son Samuel, b. Ung Ostra, 22 Jan 1877; + father-in-law, DEUTSCH, Israel, b. Holleschau, 8 Nov 1808; and nephew, REDLICH, Josef, b. Holleschau, 18
2 CONC 82.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 7 Dec 1837, Ewa [Eva] [Chawa] Weinberger, b. household #4, 4 Sep 1802, dau of Moises and Gutl (Fischl) Weinberger.  Marriage record: “Israel Deutsch, age 28, household #14, and Ewa Weinberger, age 31, m. 7 Dec 1837 [witness:
2 CONC   Jakob Deutsch].”  She was living in 1857, but deceased by 1869.
