2 CONT Abraham Zwillinger, b. household #47, 4 May 1819, “son of Markus Zwillinger and Gutl Hersch”, d. in Vienna, 20 Apr 1902, age 83.   His occupation was that of engineer.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. in Holesov, 13 Sep 1849, Schendel [Netti] Wolf, b. Holesov, 25 Nov 1817, dau of Herman and Anna (Fischer) Wolf and sister of noted educator Dr. Gerson Wolf.  Marriage record: “Abraham Zwillinger, age 30, son of familianten M
2 CONC arkus Zwillinger and Guttel geb. Hersch, and Schendel recte Netty Wolf, age 31 and ¾ , dau of familianten Hermann Wolf and Anna geb. Fischer, m. 13 Sep 1849.”  She d. in Vienna, Austria, 13 Mar 1901, age 83.
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  ZWILLINGER, Abraham, b. 1819; wife Netti, b. 1818; son Josef, b. 1850; son Markus, b. 1852; son Samuel [twin], b. 1854, son Leopold [twin], b. 1854; and dau Amalia, b. 1856.  
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1869, he and his family were living in Vienna -- Holesov, 1869: [Wien – ppg. 682-683] ZWILLINGER, Abraham, b. 1819; wife Netti, b. 1818; son Josef, b. 1850; son Emil /:Markus:/, b. 1852; son Samuel, b. 1854; son Leopold, b. 185
2 CONC 4; dau Amalia, b. 1856; son Hermann, b. 1858; and son Bernard, b. 1863. 
