1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth record:  https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000141885242786
2 CONT
2 CONT Ignatz [Isak] Zwillinger, b. in Holesov, 11 Sep 1821, youngest son of Markus and Gutel (Hersch) Zwillinger, died in Budapest, Hungary, 10 Oct 1897, age 76.  As his father's younger son -- with very few legal rights -- he left Mora
2 CONC via in early adulthood and moved to Hungary.  He lived first in Ujpest (just outside Budapest) before eventually moving to Pest.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 1st, Zirl [Cirl], b. Holesov, c1830.  She died in childbirth on 15 Sep 1855.  Her infant daughter was named in her honor.  Her gravestone is still standing in Holesov — “Cirl, wife of Jicchak Zwillinger”.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 2nd, 1856, Magdalena [Magdolna] [Lea] [Leni] Grunbaum, b. Leipnik, Moravia, 6 Aug 1828, dau of Nathan Jacob Grunbaum [d. Leipnik, 12 Aug 1839] and Maria [Mundl] (Ehrenfest) Grunbaum; d. Budapest, 30 Dec 1893.  "Magdolna Zwil
2 CONC linger szul. Grunbaum, age 61, wife of Ignacz Zwillinger, born in Leipnik, Moravia, d. in Pest, 30 Dec 1893."
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  ZWILLINGER, Ignaz, b. 1822; wife Magdalena, b. 1832; dau Cacelia, b. 1855; plus [illegible female], b. 1849 [not a daughter]
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov census, 1869 — Pest, Ungarn:  ZWILLINGER, Ignatz, b, 1822; wife Magdalena, b. 1832; dau Zili, b. 1855; plus FUCHS, Salomon, b. 1841 [*younger Zwillinger children inadvertently omitted]
2 CONT
2 CONT Repeated in Budapest, but with more complete information -- Pest, 1869: [Band 3 – pg. 866/925] ZWILLINGER, Ignatz, fabriktbeamter, b. Holesan, Mahren, 1822; wife, ZWILLINGER, Magdalena, b. Leipnik, Mahren, 1832; son, ZWILLINGER, N
2 CONC athan, b. Pest, 1859; nephew, ZWILLINGER, Jakob, “schneider gasalla”, b. Udvard, 1846; daughter, ZWILLINGER, Cecilia, b. Holesan, 1855; daughter, ZWILLINGER, Maria, b. Pest, 1858; and daughter, ZWILLINGER, Bertha, b. Pest, 1861.
