1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel Zwillinger was named in honor of his paternal grandfather, Samuel Zwillinger (1757-1806).  He was a furrier, and resided in household #14 in Holesov's Jewish quarter.  He is seen in both the 1857 and the 186
2 CONC 9 censuses.  He died there in 1882, age 55.
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  Samuel Zwillinger, born 1827, day labourer, Holesov #14; his wife, Eva, born 1832; their daughter, Maria, born 1857
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869:  Samuel Zwillinger, born 1828 (error for 1827), businessman with furs, Holesov #14; his wife, Eva, born 1833 (error for 1832); their daughter, Amalia, born 1858 (error for 1857); their daughter, Mina, born 1859; the
2 CONC ir daughter, Zilli, born 1869
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. Eva Steinhart, b. House No. 27, Holesov, 1 Jan 1833, dau of Nachum and Dwora (Khon) Steinhart; d. Vienna, Austria, 5 Aug 1919, age 87.  
