1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was born in Leipnik on 5 May 1818.  Her original birth entry switched her name with that of her mother’s, but the mistake was later corrected.  Her birth name was Rebeka, but she was “Rosa” when she married in 
2 CONC 1849, and “Rosi” in the 1857 Holesov census.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage record:  “Lipman Dienstag, age 72, widower, familiant No. 59, and Rosa Schönthal, age 26, dau of Leipniker familianten Michal Schönthal and Eva geb. Redlich, m. 29 Mar 1849 [witness:  Pinkus Redlich, familianten].”
2 CONT
2 CONT Following Lipmann Dienstag’s death in 1861, she m. 2nd, c1864, widower Jacob Zwillinger (1793-1879).
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in Holesov on 21 Jul 1903.
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1857:  [household #46a.] DIENSTAG, Lippmann, b. 1775; wife Rosi, b. 1821.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1869:  [ppg. 50-51] ZWILLINGER, Jakob, b. 1794; wife Rosi, b. Leipnik, 1825; grandson, KAPP, Wilhelm, b. Brusni, 1860.  [Insert:  “Wilhelm Kapp, b. 26 Feb 1860, son of Moses Kapp and Sali geb. Zwillinger”].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1880:  [pg. 192] ZWILLINGER, Rosi, b. Leipnik, 1823, widow; with HIRSCH, Zili, b. Martinitz, 1816, widow.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1890:  [pg. 136] ZWILLINGER, Rachel, b. Leipnik, 1830, with two boarders.  [*Both her first name and her year of birth are erroneously listed in this record].
2 CONT
2 CONT Holesov, 1900:  ZWILLINGER, Rosa, b. 6 Apr 1818 – in Dosaudel household.
