1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob Zwillinger, b. Zsambek, 1817, died in Miskolc, Borsod-Abauj-Zemplen, Hungary, 22 Mar 1869, in his 52nd year of age. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The younger of two sons in his father’s household in 1821-22 and in 1830-31. In 1836, he is seen living in Pest -- Pest, 1836: [pg. 693/702] ZWILLINGER, Jac., age 19 yrs., b. Zsambek, in household of Tobias Grun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 1st, in Zsambek, c1850, Josepha [Pessel] [Peppi] Knepler, b. Zsambek, 1824, d. Pest, 18 Nov 1854, age 30 yrs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 2nd, in Pest, 25 Feb 1855, Franziska [Feigl] “Fanni”] Beck, b. Bosnia, 1825; d. Miskolc, 23 Aug 1871, age 46 yrs.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT marriage: https://www.jewishgen.org/databases/jgdetail_2.php  ZWILLINGER, Jacob BEK, Franziska	 /  ()      /  ()	32 28	25-Feb-1855 Pest Budapest Local Gov't Pest-Pilis-Solt-Kiskun	Groom widower from Zsambek. Bride from Bosnia. Wit
2 CONC ness Elias KOHNER, Joseph LOWE	LDS 642974, Vol. 28 37-12
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: marriage: https://www.jewishgen.org/databases/jgdetail_2.php Pest Budapest Local Gov't Pest-Pilis-Solt-Kiskun Groom widower from Zsambek. Bride from Bosnia. Witness Elias KOHNER, Joseph LOWE LDS 642974, Vol. 28 37-12
