1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jakob Zwillinger, b. Ajka Rendek [Ajkarendeki Tanyak], Veszprem, 1814, was the son of David (?) Zwillinger and the grandson of Joseph Zwillinger (1760-1836). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1848, he was living with his second wife and his children in Sandorhaz, Zala megye, Hungary. Sandorhaz, Zala, 1848: CZIVILINGER, Jakab, age 34 yrs., b. Ajka Rendek, Veszprem; second wife, (MURKI) Nani, age 38 yrs., b. Merenye; 
2 CONC son David, age 10 yrs., b. Sz. Laszlo; dau Rozi, age 7 yrs., b. Sz. Laszlo; dau Anna, age 5 yrs., b. Sz. Laszlo; dau Borbala, age 2 yrs., b. Sz. Laszlo; KUPPERSTEIN, Farkas, age 17 yrs., orphan, b. Sz. Laszlo, raised by Jakab; and
2 CONC  KUPPERSTEIN, Josef, age 15 yrs., orphan,  b. Dios Kal, raised by Jakab. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of his first wife is unknown. His second wife Nani Murki, b. Merenye, 1810. The Kupperstein brothers were the older children of his first wife, and therefore both orphans and his stepchildren in 1848.
