1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1833, Charlotte and her first cousin Moritz [son of Lobl] were both working in the Mayer household in Pest. They were two households away from their aunt, Anna (Zwillinger) Berger, and three households away from
2 CONC  their paternal grandfather, Joseph Zwillinger (1760-1836).
2 CONT
2 CONT Pest, 1833: [p. 200/378] MAYER, Joseph, age 26; wife, Charlotte, age 25, b. Pesth; dau Rosina, age 3, b. Pesth; dau Christina, age 1 ½, b. Pesth; plus VALTNER, Ignatz, b. D. Kiraly, age 18 yrs; ZWILLINGER, Moritz, age 14 yrs., b. 
2 CONC Pesth; and ZWILLINGER, Charlotte, maid, age 15 yrs, b. Veszprem [three doors away from Joseph Zwillinger; (1760-1836), two doors away from Anna (Zwillinger) Berger (1807-1880).]
