1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Regina [Regine] [“Regi”] Zwillinger, b. 1834, died in Budapest, 1908, age 74.  Budapest Grave:  “Seifensieder Regina – szul. Zwillinger Regina, 1834-1908”.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She m. in Pest, 7 Sep 1851, Jakab Seifensieder, b. Budapest, 1825, d. Pest, 18 Nov 1889, age 64.  “Jakab Seifensieder, age 64, b. Budapest, husband of Regina (Zwillinger) Seifensieder, d. Pest, 18 Nov 1889.”  Between 1852 and 1872
2 CONC , Pest Jewish records show that she gave birth to 12 children of whom only one — the eldest, Terez (b. 1852) — survived infancy.  Eight of those births are recorded as stillborns.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Regina (Zwillinger) Seifensieder is listed as a surviving sister in the death notice of Leonora (Zwillinger) Schwarz (1829-1906).
2 CONT
2 CONT “Jacob Seifensieder, age 23, of Pest, and Regine Zwellinger, age 18, m. Pest, 7 Sep 1851 [witness:  Leopold Grunhut (uncle of the bride)].” 
2 CONT
2 CONT ROSENBERG, Ozias I. (age 45, b. Stryj, Galicia) son of Leiser & Zisel Rosenberg  married SEIFENSIEDER, Terez (age 35, b. Pest) daughter of Jakab Seifensieder & Regina (ZWILLINGER). Marriage Registration: 20-Feb-1887 (Budapest, Loc
2 CONC al Gov't). Note: Groom widower. Source: LDS 642975, Vol. 36, 08-05. 
