1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Named in honor of his paternal grandfather, Rabbi Salomon Teomim-Zwillinger (1767-1829).  He m. in Hotzenplotz, 10 Jul 1864, Ernestine [Ester] Vogl, aka Josephine Vogel, b. Leipnik, 25 Jun 1838, d. Opava-Troppau, 1
2 CONC 7 Feb 1904, age 65.  They were the parents of seven children, of whom four died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Salomon Zwillinger died in Troppau on 8 Mar 1912, age 77.  The graves of both he and his wife are still standing in Opava Jewish Cemetery.  A portion of the inscription on his stone reads as follows:  "Mr. Salomon Zwillinger, a tr
2 CONC ader from Osoblaha, was in business in Opava -- Dies at 77 years 8. iii. 1912."
2 CONT
2 CONT Opava-Troppau, 1870:  ZWILLINGER, Salomon, b. Hotzenplotz, 1834, of Troppau; wife Ernestine, b. Leipnik, 1838; son Maximilian, b. Troppau, 1868.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Opava-Troppau, 1881:  ZWILLINGER, Salomon, b. Hotzenplotz, 10 Jul 1834; wife Ernestine, b. Leipnik, 25 Jun 1838; son Max, b. Troppau, 31 Jul 1868; son Berthold, b. Troppau, 14 Aug 1873; son Julius, b. Troppau, 7 Jul 1877.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Opava-Troppau, 1891:  ZWILLINGER, Salomon, b. Troppau, 10 Jul 1834; wife Ernestine, b. Leipnik, 25 Jun 1838; son Max, b. Troppau, 31 Jul 1868; son Berthold, b. Troppau, 14 Aug 1873; son Julius, b. Troppau, 7 Jul 1877.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Opava-Troppau, 1901:  ZWILLINGER, Salomon, b. Hotzenplotz-Jagerndorf, 20 Jul 1834; wife Ernestin, b. Leipnik, 25 Jun 1838.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Opava-Troppau, 1911:  ZWILLINGER, Salomon, b. Hotzenplotz-Jagerndorf, 10 Jul 1838 [living alone].
