1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bernhard Zwillinger, b. Hotzenplotz, 25 Sep 1837, was the son of Jacob and Anna (Eisler) Zwillinger.  He was “of Troppau” when he m. in Osoblaha, 25 Feb 1873, Theresia [“Rosi”] Singer of Weisskirchen.  They were th
2 CONC e parents of four children:  Olga (b. 1874), Dr. Jakob (b. 1876), Max Joseph (1878-1946), and Richard.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870, Bernhard Zwillinger was still single and sharing a household in Troppau with his widowed mother and youngest sister Ernestine (b. 1849):
2 CONT
2 CONT Opava-Troppau, 1870:  ZWILLINGER, Bernhard, b. Hotzenplotz, 1838; mother Anna, widow, b. Hotzenplotz, 1805; and Zwillinger, Ernestina, b. 1858 [*error for 1849]. 
