1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi Yehoshua Heschel Charif (born in Vilna around 1580 and died in 5408-1648 in Krakow) was one of the students of the Maharam of Lublin and of Rabbi Yehoshua Falk. He served in Grodno from Elul 5394 (1634) until
2 CONC  5396 (1636), and later on in Premisla, Lvov, and Krakow, where he lead the great Yeshiva with Rabbi Yom Tov Lipman Heller, the author of "Tosafot Yom Tov".
2 CONT
2 CONT He had many students, and was known for his book "Meginei Shlomo" which included novellae on many tractates of the Talmud. Aside from this, he is known for his book of responsa "Pnei Yehoshua". Teivils, grandfather, Rabbi Yehoshua
2 CONC  Heschel Charif (born in Vilna around 1580 and died in 5408-1648 in Krakow) was one of the students of the Maharam of Lublin and of Rabbi Yehoshua Falk. He had many students, and was known for his book [http://hebrewbooks.org/4097
2 CONC 7 '''"Meginei Shlomo"'''] which included novellae on many tractates of the Talmud. Aside from this, he is known for his book of responsa [http://hebrewbooks.org/22440 '''"Pnei Yehoshua".''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources
