2 CONT Rabbi and cabalist; born in Poland 1726; died at Nikolsburg April 28, 1778; son of R. Zvi Hirsch Horowitz, rabbi of Czortkow, and brother of R. Phinehas Horowitz of Frankfort-on-the-Main. A disciple of Dov Baer of Meseritz, he was
2 CONC  a devotee of the Kabala; and this brought him the reputation of a saint, to which he owed his call to Nikolsburg in 1773, after he had been rabbi of Ryczywol in Poland. In 1775 he was appointed chief rabbi of the province of Mora
2 CONC via. Horowitz's fame as a saint increased; and his arrival was supposed to have broken a long spell of drought. In Nikolsburg he established for those observing the Ḥasidic rite a synagogue ("Chasidimschul") which existed to the e
2 CONC nd of the nineteenth century. His cabalistic homilies on the Pentateuch were published under the title "Dibre Shemu'el" (Lemberg, c. 1870).
2 CONT
2 CONT
