1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Article about Rabbi Boruch Shapiro's death: https://www.nli.org.il/en/newspapers/mgd/1877/09/12/01/article/12/?srpos=4&e=-------en-20--1-byDA-img-txIN%7CtxTI--------------1
2 CONT HaMAGID NEWSPAPER
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is the translation of the article below thanks to the help of a newly found cousin Dror Bereznitsky who is my 5th cousin once removed.  He is connected via Rabbi Baruchs sister Gutka.
2 CONT
2 CONT The obituary is in old style Hebrew, the translation is more or less:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Miechów(Kielce district), The sound of crying is heard from the city of Czyzew as the noble person, the righteous Rabbi, the great genius Baruch Szapiro has been taken from us. A descendant of Rash"i, passed away on 22 of Av at t
2 CONC he age of 67.
2 CONT Left thousands of heartbroken followers who sheltered under his shadow.
2 CONT All who heard his name in far away lands are mourning his death, great grief is upon the jews everywhere the bad news is spread as a great man has died.
2 CONT Torah and work were his whole life, thousands had sheltered under his wings as he guided them and gathered them under the wings of the divine presence to show them the right path. 
2 CONT We shall be comforted as he left us a blessing - his son the wise Rabbi Nathan Szapiro of Pilica, worthy of taking his father's throne and leading his followers.
2 CONT May the Lord comfort these mourners among the rest of the mourners of Zion and Jerusalem including myself who is writing those words as I am heartbroken.
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel Szternfeld Ha-Kohen
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1868 he became a Rebbi "Rebbe" for the chasidim.  His wife worked.  His official leadership started in1875 Czwew
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This record is our family but no idea where it belongs.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/jednostka/-/jednostka/6085179
2 CONT
2 CONT Files on the care of minor children [i.e. Zysia Lejba, Moszek-Mordka, Rasza Mirla Szapiro and the others] by Jankel Icek Szapiro 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signature
2 CONT 62/433/0/2/10
2 CONT
2 CONT Dates
2 CONT 1916 - 1917
2 CONT Archives
2 CONT State Archives in Siedlce
2 CONT Team
2 CONT Commune Court in Siedlce
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://bloodandfrogs-com.translate.goog/wp-content/uploads/encyclopedia/poland/kirkuty/czyzew_osada.htm?_x_tr_sl=pl&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=sc
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT NEW INFO IN YIZKOR BOOK of Czyzew: 10/2016 My Aleksander Shtibl http://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/Czyzew/czy0225.html by Berl Szajes/Tel Aviv Translated by Gloria Berkenstat Freund
2 CONT
2 CONT Sector 32 Row 4 no 16
2 CONT
2 CONT I spent my most wonderful young years in this shtibl [small Hasidic house of prayer; shtiblekh is the plural]. Everything I saw there, heard and experienced is deeply etched in my memory. It was a time when it seemed to us that th
2 CONC e Aleksander shtibl had developed together with the shtetl [town], as if it had existed since the origin of the community in Czyzewo. Later it became clear to me that the Jewish settlement in Czyzewo consisted of superb Jews, scho
2 CONC lars and craftsmen who studied Torah, and led a warm Jewish life much earlier than the rise of the Hasidic movement. It was just after the death of the old “Wurker” that the later Aleksander Hasidim began to develop. Around 100 ye
2 CONC ars ago, Reb Yeheil Danciker, the son of Reb Feywele Gricer, a grandson of the great Warsaw rich man, scholar and misnagid [opponent of Hasidism], Reb Tzwi Hersh Danciker, took over the management and created the first minyon [ten
2 CONC  men needed for prayer; minyonim in the plural] of scholarly young men, who were strong adherents of the new customs and began going in his path, singing the nigumim [melodies], keeping to his manner of praying.
2 CONT
2 CONT At that time Czyzewo began to sense the differences between the Ger and Aleksander Hasidim. Reb Borukh Szapira advised and urged traveling to the Sfas Emes [the Ger Rebbe Yehudah Leib Alter].
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/Czyzew/czy0273.html Czyzewo was situated on the border area of Lithuania and Poland, between the vibrant Hassidic centers of Poland on the one side, and the fortresses of the Lithuanian Misnagdim on
2 CONC  the other side. Nevertheless, Czyzewo itself was a bastion of Hassidism. It had many Hassidim of Ger, Aleksander, Amszynow, and others. At an earlier time, it was also the honorable dwelling place of the Admor Rabbi Baruch Szapir
2 CONC a of holy blessed memory, the student of Rabbi Mendele of Kotzk of holy blessed memory. He led a Hassidic community there. The influence of the Hassidim upon the town was great. They spread Torah and awe of G-d in the town, and th
2 CONC ey played a very prominent role in communal life. In reality, they were the hewers of the image of Czyzewo in the full sense of the word, until such time as the representatives of other organizations and movements appeared, and th
2 CONC e town turned into a town with both religious and secular factions together. There were branches of Agudas Yisrael, Mizrachi, Zionists, Beitar, Poale Zion, and others. Each one of these groups attracted a different circle and fact
2 CONC ion, and tended to its own needs.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/Czyzew/czy0077.html At the beginning of the 19th century, the Hasidic wind began to penetrate the town. At that time the ruling of society went over to the Hasidim and dominant among them were the G
2 CONC er Hasidim and they cooperated in getting Rabbi Boruch Szapiro of Szcuszyn ( Stuczyn in Idish) to settle in town. He was one of the followers of the Kocker court and and a supporter of the later Ger rebbe.
2 CONT
