1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Find-a-grave memorial shows birth date of Dec. 24, 1812, and death date of Dec. 8, 1900:  
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/20722/henry-russell
2 CONT ________________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Russell was a singer and composer.  The BBC broadcast a programme devoted to his life and works on 13th August 1972.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born at Sheerness on 12th December 1872. (Source - JHSE XXIV page 162.  His mother was a niece of Solomon Hirschell, the Chief Rabbi.  Members of his family were prominent members of the Western Synagogue.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of eight he sang at the Brighton Pavilion before King George IV. About 1830 he went to Milan and studied under Rossini.  On his return he was chorus master at Her Majesty's Theatre, and then went to America for several 
2 CONC years.  While in America he campaigned for the abolition of slavery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He composed and published over 800 songs, and is best known today for "Life on the Ocean Wave", the regimental march of the Royal Marines.
2 CONT
2 CONT Russell was married twice, the first time to a Christian and then to Miss De Lara, who was Jewish.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Jewish Chronicle, 14th December, 1900.
2 CONT
2 CONT (JMM)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
