1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi Mordechai Rosen (1881-1939, Otzar Ha-Rabanim 14024), of Ruzhyn-Chortkov Chassidim, son in law of Rabbi Ya'akov Meir Bleich. Was ordained as teacher by the Maharsha"m and by Rabbi Meir Arik. Served as rabbi of
2 CONC  Monastrytchaz, settled in Vienna after World War I, where served as rabbi. In 1938 was appointed Av-Beit–Din of Vienna, following Rabbi Yossef Babad's flee to Holland due to Nazi threat. Was arrested by the Nazis in 1939 and a fe
2 CONC w days later his wife was informed that if she pays delivery fees she will get his ashes. (https://www.kedem-auctions.com/content/letter-rabbi-mordechai-rosen-%E2%80%93-dayan-and-moreh-zedek-vienna)
