1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Second marriage Szczebrzeszyn (RC) 1819 №63 https://szukajwarchiwach.pl/35/1930/0/1/41/skan/save/N3X2Kh3Qg4e0S2yf47DrdQ
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Szczebrzeszyn 1831 №7
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/skan/-/skan/96a2ec823cd5a8f3478511a9965fde4bc1c7e032f472f16cc11cf19e5fbbffaa
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Lejbus' Szper wife Mirla (you ancestor GGG...grandmother) died after giving the birth to their last child - in 1819. Widowed Lejbko immediately remarried to another woman (also widow) Leja Wilenz (I suppose that she came from Wiln
2 CONC o - according to her surname).
2 CONT After Lejbko's death this Leja remarried her third(!) marriage to...my GGGGGreat grandfather's (Lublin's maternal line of my grandfather) nephew in Lublin - Morgansztern. He was very famous Rabbi in Lublin. He was the son of my GG
2 CONC GGGreat aunt Rejna-Pessa Goldrajch (Morgansztern) from Lublin -- the very old Lewy dynasty in that town that are buried on the very first cemetery there.
2 CONT NB: The surname WILANZ means the origin from WOŁYŃ- the region of the Western Ukraine - Laia Wilanc came from Włodzimierz Wolynski according to her marriage documents.
2 CONT ————————
2 CONT The document about the fact of property purchase ( land)  in Kolo from Berko Szrajber in 1806 for a price of 50 PZl 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/skan/-/skan/fc98a8d8272778e5ca9a7eba37773f126692885a201185ba2240637b70483f2c
2 CONT ———————-/-
2 CONT 1806: The document about property exchange against the land owned by Lejbus Szper and 150 PZl supplement  with Benedict Wyrostkiewicz lived in the house on near the Brama Zamoyska in the town center
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/skan/-/skan/580ced2a18d6c93b827786e864145426fd5f459fb7aba68e6f3d8786a3ec2a39
2 CONT ————————-
2 CONT 20/5/1806 Lejbus recognised as the legal owner of the vineyard purchased by himself from the descendants of deceased Gerszon Deutscher
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/skan/-/skan/4870c117ba7ca64994a308a3974047942e72a3fb0cac228f5d93614cf04648ad
2 CONT —————————
2 CONT The contract of purchase itself: the price was 1100 PZl 
2 CONT The property was situated next to the distillery of Icek Kandel and Moszko Szper - on the river Wieprz
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/skan/-/skan/2db05154027c775bdf2d646181eee1eadcd7fcf712e57e4d16c393cc2dec06cc
2 CONT —————————
2 CONT The contract of common purchasing the big property №10 on the central Market place (Rynek) in 1805 by brothers(???) Moszko and Lejbus Szper for 6400 PZl from Walenty and Agneszka Stoczkowskich - property was previously owned in 17
2 CONC 76 by Pinkwas Israelowicz. The brick made house was situated between two town gates - Brama Zamoyska and Brama Bilgorajska. The building had cellar, two kitchens, wodenmade toilets and two more brickwall separate constructions att
2 CONC ached to the house. 
2 CONT 1st page:
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/skan/-/skan/f65d8fdc9fa60dcf4646ae31e37ac14bcbcf63c6adb47954ed0e06911656f6aa
2 CONT 2d page:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/skan/-/skan/8a12822da080fbf8044bb18c4915a0b10db1ea674e415032846a7c40142c48ff
2 CONT ———————————————————————
2 CONT Evidence Lejbus Szper was one of the major property owner in the area of Tomaszow, Krasnostaw (one of the most important taxpayers)
2 CONT 1812 Lublin notary archive № 251
2 CONT https://skanoteka.genealodzy.pl/index.php?op=pg&id=3977&se=&sy=21&kt=&plik=035.jpg&x=41&y=30&zoom=3.38
2 CONT ———————————————————————-
2 CONT
2 CONT The evidence that Mendel Ettinger, Lejbus Szper (Szczebrzeszyn) , Abraham Montag (Szczebrzeszyn), Szmul Erlich (Zamosc), Hersz Rajs (Tomaszower Rabbi Eyzyk Rajs[feld] son - Tomaszów Lubelski and Wolf Fliegel (Lublin) supplied in 1
2 CONC 812 100 tons of meat to Napoleon’s army that was quartered in Zamosc. as part of the anti-Russian campaign of 1812-1813. 
2 CONT In early civil records Lejbus Szper mentioned as the “liwerant armii” that on Polish/French slang means supplier. 
2 CONT The notary archive of Lublin 1812 №№611, 612, 613
2 CONT https://skanoteka.genealodzy.pl/index.php?op=pg&id=3977&se=&sy=21&kt=&plik=045.jpg&x=1819&y=318&zoom=1.73
