1 NAME Benjamin Bushka /Fischel/ of Zamosc
2 GIVN Benjamin Bushka
2 NSFX of Zamosc
2 _MARNM Fischel
2 NICK Fischel-klausner
1 NAME R' Benjamin Fischel Bushka of Zamosc
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1705
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Possible error:
2 CONT
2 CONT Horowitz (Kitvei HaGeonim, p. 64-5) states that Benyamin may have been  a son-in-law of R. Yakov (A.B.D. Ludmir, d. 1730) rather than a son, and Wunder (Elef Margoliot) agrees.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duckess (Iweh LeMoshav, p. 77) states that Benyamin was a paternal grandson of Aryeh Leib "the Tall" [he is listed here as a paternal greatgrandson] and a maternal grandson of R. Saul Katzenellenbogen (and thus a son of R' Yakov).
2 CONC " [He is listed here that way, suggesting a generational error on one side.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Tzvi Hirsh Zamosc, listed here as Benyamin's son, claims this relationship in his book, Tiferent Tzvi (Lvov, 1811) that R. Saul Katzenellenbogen is his maternal grandfather. Thus, if he is indeed Benyamin's son, Benyamin would be 
2 CONC a son of R. Saul Katzenellenbogen and, as Duckess claims, a paternal grandson of Aryeh Leib "the Tall."
2 CONT
2 CONT Moreover, Horowitz (LeToledot haKehilot bePolin) states that he was the brother of Tzvi, author of Tiferet Tzvi who, according to Hebrewbooks.org, was the son of Israel Binyamin Bishko/Bushka.
2 CONT
2 CONT For his son, Ephraim Fischel, Rosenstein refers to Horowitz, LeKorot HaYehudim BePolin, p. 264. For Moses Solomon Zalman and his son-in-law, he refers to S. Yevnin, Nachalat Olamim #10 & #56.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Horowitz (Kitvei HaGeonim, p. 64-5) provides a list of Benjamin's descendants.
