2 SURN הורוביץ
2 NICK האראוויץ
2 NICK ראש הברזל
1 NAME הרב עזריאל הלוי הורוביץ, אב"ד לובלין - 'דער אייזנער קאפ'
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lublin
3 STAE Lublin Voivodeship
3 CTRY Poland
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1733
2 ADDR
3 CITY Zamosc
3 STAE Lublin Voivodeship
3 CTRY Poland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 NOV 1818
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lublin
3 STAE Lublin Voivodeship
3 CTRY Poland
1 OCCU Chief Rabbi
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Death Lublin 20/11/ 1818 - death record from the 21st of November 1818 (Roman Catholic Archive of St. Michail Cathedral)  №406 - page 199 (right side on the top)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.szukajwarchiwach.gov.pl/skan/-/skan/c66cde0c19819d4dccdb76523ffe2ee3c1a2ea169a1c74df0b595eb37751be14
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the A.B.D. of Lublin from 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was called the "Rosh HaBarzel" in hebrew or "Eisene Kup" in yiddish. In English, this means Iron Head. He died on Cheshvan 22 5579 ( Oct / Nov 1818). (Information received from Azriel Horowitz.)
2 CONT
2 CONT NB: the evidence he had the double name comes from Notary documents of 1811 (RC Archive of Lublin) № 284
2 CONT https://skanoteka.genealodzy.pl/index.php?op=pg&id=3976&se=&sy=13&kt=&plik=025.jpg&x=897&y=658&zoom=2.7
2 CONT https://metbox3.genealodzy.pl/23/metryka_get.php?op=download&dir=mvmw6kq5_fkfq7-pOuVy12VrIiojr-5-Vobp1YMBs8o,&znak=QetVSxxqFsEFAs_WV9Y71A,,&plik=005.jpg
2 CONT There are many more other cases in which R’ Israel [Azriel] Horowicz mentioned under double name ISRAEL '''DAWID''' HOROWICZ RABIN LUBELSKI. The reason he never appeared under his second name Dawid in civil records is unknown yet.
2 CONC  This fact could be a point for a further research: his patronymic Dov/Ber would have been used as BERKOWICZ. 
2 CONT However, his tombstone and his writings only give his name as Azriel. Additionally, he had a son name David which is implausible under Ashkenazic Jewish custom had that been his name too.
2 CONT ——————————————————
2 CONT The notary Archive of Lublin 1819 №575: names of all children-descendants are mentioned including the married names of his daughters. Further information/ research needed about Silberfeld family from Krakow. 
2 CONT https://notariaty.genealodzy.pl/index.php?op=pg&id=3977&se=&sy=24&kt=&plik=032.jpg&x=87&y=68&zoom=2.4
