1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Related to the Trachtenberg family of Berdychiv which built Gur-Aryeh's paper mill.   [Source: Harry Sapir]
2 CONT
2 CONT On the List of Employees of Accountable Enterprises, part of the 1909 Radomysl area tax records, six members of the Horenstein family are listed including Gur-Aryeh, Taube's husband.  In addition, Mark Lav. Horovitz was listed as 
2 CONC one of two non-Horenstein members of the Revision Commission of the sugar factory, suggesting that he may have been related to Taube.  (The other non-Horenstein member, Idel Fridr[ichovich?], appears to have been a Horenstein cous
2 CONC in.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Her registration town is listed on the 1889 Marriage Register for Bolechow as "Galicia."
