1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nokhum MINC's Factory
2 CONT
2 CONT The second son-in-law of the wealthy man Isaac Zabludowski, Nokhem MINC, was a Jew, a scholar, a follower of the Enlightenment and a great man of aristocratic descent. His father, the rabbi, the sagacious scholar, Orish MINC, was 
2 CONC the 15th generation of the MINC family. He had six sons and three daughters. All of his sons as well as his sons-in-law were very educated, followers of the Enlightenment and rich men. Reb Menakhem Nokhum MINC was his sixth son an
2 CONC d also a distinguished Torah scholar. His first wife was Chaya Frume, the daughter of a rich man from Bialoystok; his third wife was Yokheved, daughter of the rabbi and great man, Mr. Zalmen Bornsztajn.[26] He died in 5626 [1866],
2 CONC  a year after his father-in-law's death. He received the stately courtyard on Kilinski Street opposite the palace (now the “Palas” Theater) from his father-in-law after his father-in-law's death. There he established a group of fa
2 CONC ctories. He erected a Beis-Midrash and also a bathhouse with a mikvah [ritual bath] for himself there at the same time.[27] He had seven sons: They were referred to as the “golden MINCs” in the city. All of them were educated and 
2 CONC studious. One of his grandsons was a well-known professor of surgery in Russia; he is now a professor in Riga. None of his family remains in Bialystok, except for one son, completely deranged, who subsisted in the old age home. Hi
2 CONC s sister, Mikhel, FRYDLANSKI wife, in Petersburg, would support him.After the factory closed, it was rented to Malka Reyzl's two sons-in-law, Mordekhai-Chaim HAJLPERIN (later the Jewish public notary), Avraham ZUSMAN and their par
2 CONC tner, Leib RASZKIN, who was an employee of Malka Reyzl. The factory and the courtyard were later sold to FRISZ, the manufacturer, from him to LITERER for production by wage earners. During war time [First World War] – for the “Pal
2 CONC as” Theater. The courtyard was divided into parcels. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Page 32] 
2 CONT
2 CONT It would be nice if the person who added this text will  add his or her  name here and when this text was written , further more page 32 in which book??? Nehirah Kadosh
