2 CONT LEVITAN, MARY. On Monday, February 1, 1937, at her residence 3044 14th st. nw., MARY LEVITAN, beloved wife of Max Levitan and devoted mother of Mrs. Samuel Sperling; of New York: Miss Sara Levitan, Miss Rebecca Levitan, Mrs. Reube
2 CONC n Klein, Barnum A., Joseph S., Simon W. and Maurice Levitan.  She is also survived by one brother Herman S. Robbin. Funeral from the chapel of Bernard Danzansky, 3501 14th st. nw., on Tuesday, February 2, at 10:30 a.m. Interment A
2 CONC das Israel Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mary Levitan Dies at Home Here
2 CONT
2 CONT The Washington Post (1877-1954); Feb 2, 1937; ProQuest Historical Newspapers The Washington Post (1877 - 1992)
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 4
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mary Levitan, 72, of 3044 Fourteenth street northwest, wife of Max Levitan, clothier, died yesterday morning at her home.
2 CONT
2 CONT A resident of Washington for 45 years, Mrs. Levitan came originally from Russia.  Surviving her are four sons, Barnum A., Joseph S., Simon M. and Maurice Levitan; four daughters, Mrs. Samuel Sperling of New York; Mrs. Reuben Klein
2 CONC  and Misses Sarah and Rebecca Levitan; ten grandchildren and one great-grandchild.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at Denzansky's undertaking establishment this morning at 10:30 o'clock, with burial in Adas Israel Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joe Lonstein:
2 CONT
2 CONT Miriam Brocha bat Rabbi Boruch Mordechai
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910 Census - mother is "Sarah Robbins", a mother of 8 children with 4 living in 1910.  A widow, born in 1835, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Entered US in 1890 with Pearl and Sarah - 1900 Census.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 10/19/1864
