1 NOTE {geni:about_me} KRIGER, Izrel-Aba	son of Vulf, -  Golde, -  - born	11/1/1888 10 Sivan 	Dichuny  Panevezys  Kaunas 	Mohel : Zalman KANTOR, Father registered in Krekenava
2 CONT
2 CONT Yisroel Abba KRIEGER 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 1880 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Channah ELKA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 1885
2 CONT
2 CONT  The Rav Was born in Shpeishuk, a small village near Kovno, Lithuania where His father Rav Chaim Zev server as Rav. At the young age of 8, the Rav was sent to the yeshiva in Eishishok to study. His After bar mitzvah he Traveled to
2 CONC  Jerusalem where he Entered the study hall of Rav Yehoshua Leib Diskin, Diligently studying for five years. In 1890 he returned to Europe and settled in Dvinsk where he became a disciple of Rev Meir Simcha HaKohen. Two years Later
2 CONC  Around Was he appointed the Rav of Kosherdari and soon after Frankfurt am Main. Due to His Lack of success n Germany he Traveled to American and Settled in Boston, Massachusetts where he Was appointed as Rav and a authoritative m
2 CONC ember of the Agudath Harabonim.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among His writings are:
2 CONT * [http://hebrewbooks.org/3131 China Dchaye חינא דחיי] (Pietrokov, 1908)
2 CONT * [http://hebrewbooks.org/968 Lirtzonchem Tizbechuhu לרצונכם תזבחוהו] (Pietrokov, 1908
2 CONT * [http://hebrewbooks.org/39089 Olah Lyafeh עולה ליפה] (Pietrokov, 1911) and posthumously: 
2 CONT * Taanugei Yisroel, 2 Vol. (Brooklyn, 1981)
2 CONT * [http://hebrewbooks.org/21411 Kedushas Bas Yisroel קדושת בת ישראל] (Brooklyn, 1982)
2 CONT * Yad Yisroel (Brooklyn, 1985). In addition the Rav was a regular contributor to the Hapardes Rabbinical Periodical.
