1 CONT G5.7. Deborah, married R. Naftali Hirsch Gunzburg as his first wife. He  was A.B.D. of Pinsk and Slutzk, and died in 1687. Deborah was from the second marriage. His first wife was Deborah's cousin, Rebecca, daughter of Judah Wahl 
1 CONC (G4.6. below). Deborah was also married to R. Jacob Weil, A.B.D.  Brest and Lublin, son of Ephraim Naftali Hirsch (Herz) Weil, A.B.D. Ludmir.  Herz's father was R. Jonah Weil with the title of Oberrabbiner of Burgau,  Schwaben and
1 CONC  Schweiz, with his seat in Gunzburg, son of R. Jacob Weil,  Landesrabbiner of Bavaria, son of the MaHaRaM Weil in Ulm, son of R. Jacob Weil (the prominent scholar known as MaHaRIY, died before 1456) of Nuremburg, son of Judah.
0 @N6000000003327798375@ NOTE
1 CONT G5.3. Nahum, A.B.D. Slutzk, was from the second marriage, having been  named after his maternal grandfather, R. Nahum of Ludmir.
0 @N6000000003327798413@ NOTE
1 CONT G5.8. Saul, named after his grandfather, Saul Wahl, married the daughter  of Elijah, A.B.D. of Wegrow, author of Brit HaLevi (Lublin 1645), son of R. Abraham HaLevi Ettinge (of Vienna, died in 1637) and his wife Feigele, daughter 
1 CONC of Samuel Phoebus, son of R. Aaron Moses Teomim. Samuel Phoebus  was a brother of Isaiah Teomim mentioned below, G5.9. Elijah's brother was R. Leib Ettinge, below G5.12. R. Abraham Ettinge was the son of R. Mordecai Segal (HaLevi)
1 CONC  from Ettingen, Bavaria, founder of the family. Another brother to Leib and Elijah was R. Naftali Herz Ettinge, a doctor, two of whose  sons were also doctors, and a third son was the famous Court Jew and Primator  of Prague, Abra
1 CONC ham Aaron Lichtenstadt (died 1702).
