1 CONC ola (4 miles) and Krok (10). It is situated on theShoshava River and 7 miles from a train station. The 3 mainstreets were Shadova, Pashushva and Krok. The Jewish settlementin 1921 had 250 people. In 1923 235. They made their livin
1 CONC g from small shopsand crafts. Market place was Tuesday. Prior to the Holocaust theJewish population was down to about 20 families. The cheder,cemetary, rabbi and shochet all served the Jews of nearby Baisigola.
